ry action is rebindable on the standard Controls screen)\n466:### 4.2 Glyphs and prompts (`03-glyphs.js`)\n481:### 4.3 Screens (big, sparse, one decision per screen; never dense web-style tables)\n526:### 4.4 In-game HUD (canvas, anchored to `r.W` / `r.H`, inside 4% overscan margins)\n544:### 4.5 Touch-only devices\n555:### 4.6 Settings (the engine's standard screens plus ours in group \"Game\"; Sound gets \"Voices\")\n573:### 4.7 Camera\n593:## 5. Systems\n597:### 5.1 Hero, intent and traversal (`40-hero.js`)\n651:### 5.2 Grappling hook — kaginawa (`42-grapple.js`)\n675:### 5.3 Light, shadow and cover (`30-world.js` + `50-perception.js`)\n702:### 5.4 Perception and guard minds (`50-perception.js`, `51-guard-brain.js`)\n746:### 5.5 Shadow Sight, the Ki Gauge and Ki Focus (`50-perception.js`, `70-hud.js`)\n766:### 5.6 Alarm, reinforcements, Heightened\n782:### 5.7 Silent Cuts — 静斬 (`41-silentcut.js`)\n818:### 5.8 Combat (`43-combat.js`)\n847:### 5.9 Tools and the Bento (`44-tools.js`)\n871:### 5.10 Bodies\n878:### 5.11 Enemies and civilians (`52-enemies.js`; rigs in section 6.1)\n893:### 5.12 Bosses (`53-bosses.js`)\n912:### 5.13 Escort — Tobei (`54-escort.js`, M2)\n924:### 5.14 Missions: objectives, triggers, checkpoints, timers (`60-mission.js`)\n951:### 5.15 Score, ranks, unlocks, saves (`61-score.js`)\n972:### 5.16 Story presentation (`62-story.js`, `63-cutscene.js`)\n983:### 5.17 Audio (`10-audio.js`, `11-voice.js`) — all code, no files\n1045:### 5.18 Visuals, assets, animation (engine-native look, PS1-era pixel art)\n1158:### 5.19 Attract mode (`81-attract.js`, `80-autopilot.js`)\n1194:### 5.20 Dev mode (`74-dev.js`) — pause menu → **Dev Mode** (not offered in hub sessions or attract)\n1272:### 5.21 Mission Editor — \"Workshop\" (`75-workshop.js`)\n1314:### 5.22 Multiplayer — AI Hub ghost mode, and the Shadow Trial on its own (`82-hub.js`)\n1382:### 5.23 About / Credits (title → About; paged)\n1397:## 6. Content\n1399:### 6.1 Characters and rigs (`21-rigs.js`)\n1423:### 6.2 Missions\n1431:#### Mission 0 — \"The Trial of the Second Tier\" (training; 40×28; dusk turning to night; petals; music `training`)\n1434:####################\n1435:#AAAAAA..FFFF\"\"\"\"\"\"\"#   A the Jubako-ya shop (h40)   F bamboo fence (vault)   \" bamboo grove\n1436:#AAAAAA....,,\"\"\"1\"\"\"#   1 Disciple Ume (lantern, slow loop in the grove)\n1437:#..@..........\"\"\"\"\"\"#   @ start, the back porch (Granny watches from the door)\n1438:#..PP....W.W......C.#   P planters (cover)   W low walls h30 (climb)   C kura storehouse h48\n1439:#..PP....W.W....CCCC#\n1440:#.......~~~~~...CCCC#   ~ koi pond (deep): Disciple Kiku (2) stands at the bank\n1441:#..,,,..~~~~~2..CC3C#   3 Disciple Masa below the kura's edge (the from-above mark target)\n1442:#.............t..b..#   t persimmon tree (grapple anchor)   b bait test spot (training dummy guard \"Big Daikon\")\n1443:#..:::::::::........#   : raked-gravel sparring ring (Brother Ittetsu)\n1444:#..:::::::::...dd...#   d practice dummies (combo practice)\n1445:####################\n1463:#### Mission 1 — \"Rice and Ash\" (castle town; 56×48; night; petals; music `m1`; faction Kanemori)\n1466:############################\n1467:#WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW....#   North: Kanemori's walled mansion\n1468:#W::::::::W HHHHHHHHH  W...#   : inner gravel court = Gonroku's arena\n1469:#W::::::::d d___k___H  W.T.#   H hall (enterable, roof cap): the feast; k Kanemori, 2 maids, 1 samurai\n1470:#W::::::::W H_______H  W...#   T watchtower + archer (lantern)\n1471:#WWWWWdWWWW HHHHdHHHH  W...#   d doorways\n1472:#W ~~~ ll  ,,,   CC    W...#   ~ garden pond, l stone lanterns, C kura (the strongbox: optional ledger)\n1473:#WWWWWWWWWWgWWWWWWWWWWWW...#   g front gate (2 gate guards); a side door on the east wall\n1474:#....AA..BB....BB...AA.....#   Middle: market square; ! alarm bell; samurai pair patrol;\n1475:#.AA.AA..BB.!..BB...AA.AA..#   noodle stall lights (yatai), 2 drunk civilians\n1476:#.AA........DD.......D.DD..#\n1477:#.BB..DD..AA....AA...BB....#   South: alleys and rooftops; 3 ashigaru, 1 hound in the rice-merchant yard\n1478:#.BB......AA.,,.AA...BB....#\n1479:#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#   canal (deep): arrive by boat at the east end, leave by the boat (X) at the west end\n1480:#X~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@#\n1481:############################\n1496:#### Mission 2 — \"The Fort at Kiri Lake\" (60×52; rain + lightning; music `m2`; faction Red Lantern)\n1499:##############################\n1500:#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~############.#   West: reed shore (,) and fishing huts (A); start @ and the escape boat X\n1501:#,AA,,,~~~~~~~~~#T::::::::T#.#   ~ lake channel (deep, 9 cells): archers on towers T sweep it with lanterns\n1502:#,AA,@,~~~~~~~~~#:BBB:!:CC:#.#   # fort outer wall h56 (grapple); B barracks (reinforcements); ! bell\n1503:#,,,,X,~~~~~~~~~#:BBB:::CC:#.#   C storehouses; Q bamboo cage with Tobei (north-east)\n1504:#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~#::::::::Q:#.#   w water gate (closed; lever L inside opens it: the escort route)\n1505:#,AA,,,~~~=====~w::L::::::::.#   = pier (Hotaru's arena on the escape route)\n1506:#,AA,,,~~~=====~#:::::::::::.#\n1507:#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~#T:m=r=m=r=mT#   dock: m mooring posts (3) holding rice barges r (optional: cut them loose)\n1508:##############################\n1523:#### Mission 3 — \"Moon over Kokaku\" (64×56; festival night, a huge moon; maple leaves; music `m3`; faction Kokaku + Red Lantern)\n1526:################################\n1527:#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#   outer moat (deep); start @ swimming at the south\n1528:#~##########################~~~#   # ishigaki wall h56; T corner towers (grapple anchors)\n1529:#~#T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,T#~~#   second bailey: the festival garden; lantern strings, stalls,\n1530:#~#,  stalls   ll   ll  ,,,,#~~#   6 nobles and servants (civilians) + 3 disguised Red Lanterns\n1531:#~#,  HHHH(tea pavilion) ,,,#~~#   H tea pavilion (hall): the poisoned sake flask (stopTimer objective)\n1532:#~#,  H__H   ll    ll   ,,,,#~~#\n1533:#~#WWWWWWWWWWWdWWWWWWWWWWWWW#~~#   W inner wall h30, gate d\n1534:#~#::::GGGGGGGG::::::::!::::#~~#   honmaru: keep tiers G h64 (16×16), K h112 (12×12), M h160 (8×8)\n1535:#~#::::GGKKKKGG:::::::::::::#~~#   samurai and archers on each tier's roof walkway\n1536:#~#::::GGKMMKGG:::::::::::::#~~#   the top of M = Kurogane's arena (shachihoko, moon behind)\n1537:#~#::::GGKKKKGG:::::::::::::#~~#\n1538:#~#::::GGGGGGGG:::::::::::::#~~#\n1539:#~##########################~~~#\n1540:#~~~~~~~~~~@~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#\n1541:################################\n1553:### 6.3 Enemy totals by mission (for balancing)\n1563:### 6.4 Tools: see section 5.9 (10 tools; 6 at the start, 4 unlocked by rank)\n1565:### 6.5 \"Night Delivery\" — the Shadow Trial and AI Hub round (level id `delivery`; 34×30; night; music `m1`)\n1568:#################\n1569:#~~~~~~~X~~~~~~~#   canal along the north edge; X the canal gate (exit)\n1570:#WWWWWWWdWWWWWWW#   W compound wall h30 (climb) with the canal gate d\n1571:#W..CC....T..CCW#   C two kura h48, roofs a grapple apart; T watchtower + archer (lantern)\n1572:#W..CC.......CCW#\n1573:#W,,....HHH....W#   H small hall: Sakubei counting coins (target), a clerk (civilian)\n1574:#W,,.l..H_H..l.W#   l stone lanterns (light pools); , tall grass by the wall\n1575:#W....~~~....,,W#   ~ pond (deep: dive past the samurai's beat)\n1576:#W..h.~~~......W#   h hound on a short beat by the storehouse\n1577:#WWWWWWWWWWWWWWW#\n1578:#.......@.......#   @ start outside the south wall\n1579:#################\n1589:### 6.6 Story script (tone: earnest, terse feudal drama; deadpan bento details; ASCII only)\n1701:## 7. Build order and milestones\n1722:## 8. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1745:## 9. Testing (`tests/run.mjs` — one command, failures only, one-line count)\n1747:### 9.1 The runner\n1779:### 9.2 Suites (each check uses fixed spots in test levels or the campaign maps)\n1806:### 9.3 Engine tools\n1812:### 9.4 Balance pass (M10)\n1820:### 9.5 Screenshots (only what scripts can't judge)\n1844:## 10. Final checklist (and what to write at the end)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Vs9zqMYAwbinEqiYKgwahM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
