{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2bHuJYU21aPPjgB2Qh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GtiPdkjubvn64YPq4TR1Vp","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183420__xf7f297/work/PLAN.md","limit":600},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4635,"cache_read_input_tokens":22529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4635},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"c4aa4966-272f-484b-838e-a517543042e9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:36.419Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2bHges6fgCx95eU2Zn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GtiPdkjubvn64YPq4TR1Vp":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183420__xf7f297/work/PLAN.md","limit":600}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GtiPdkjubvn64YPq4TR1Vp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins\n2\t\n3\t*An original isometric ninja stealth-action game, a playful riff on* Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins.\n4\t*Build plan for the developers (human or AI) who will build it from TASK.md and this file alone.*\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## 0. At a glance\n9\t\n10\t**Pitch.** Kasugai Province, the Sengoku era. The granaries are full and the people starve. In the shadow of Kokaku\n11\tCastle, a humble shop, the **Jubako-ya**, sells two-tier lunchboxes (jubako) to the lord's household. Its boxes have two\n12\ttiers. So does the shop: one tier for the rice and one for the blade. You play one of its two apprentices, **Sojiro**\n13\t(katana, steady) or **Kaede** (twin short blades, quick), through the night they pass their trial and become true\n14\t**Lunchbox Assassins**. The story is played straight, in the source's earnest, terse feudal-drama voice. The jokes are\n15\tdeadpan and come from the world (poisoned rice balls, rank names taken from bento grades), never from winking.\n16\t\n17\t**Core loop (one sentence, put it at the top of the game code):** take a mission at the shop, pack your bento of ninja\n18\ttools, slip into a lantern-lit night location unseen, silence guards with Silent Cuts, reach the target, survive the\n19\tboss, escape, and earn a rank that unlocks new tools.\n20\t\n21\t**Genre:** third-person ninja stealth-action, with light melee combat and boss duels.\n22\t**Perspective:** isometric third person on the engine's `iso` view (yaw 45, pitch 30), rotatable in 45-degree steps and\n23\tzoomable, with `threequarter` as a Settings alternative (\"Camera angle: Low / High\"). Tenchu's behind-the-back 3D camera\n24\tis not available in this 2D engine. Its job (limited sight, the ki sense, looking around corners) is rebuilt as\n25\t**Shadow Sight** (section 5.5): enemies the ninja can't see are hidden unless the Ki gauge senses them.\n26\t\n27\t**Scope of the demo (all required, no stubs):**\n28\t\n29\t- A training mission and three story missions, each with a boss. That is about 45 minutes of play.\n30\t- Two playable characters.\n31\t- 10 tools, packed in the bento.\n32\t- 5 guard types plus civilians and disguised enemies.\n33\t- Silent Cuts from 5 directions.\n34\t- Grappling hook, swimming and diving, body dragging, wall hugging, light and shadow, noise, alarm bells with\n35\t  reinforcements, and an escort mission.\n36\t- Ranks and unlocks, and saves.\n37\t- Story cutscenes with gibberish voices.\n38\t- Dev mode with live balance sliders.\n39\t- An attract mode.\n40\t- A Mission Editor (the \"Workshop\", after Tenchu 2's Mission Editor).\n41\t- AI Hub ghost-mode multiplayer for 1–4 players, plus its standalone twin, the Shadow Trial, where you race your own\n42\t  best ghost.\n43\t- An About/Credits screen.\n44\t\n45\t**Deliverables (names follow TASK.md's bracket pattern with GameTitle = `Bentou2`, SOURCE = `Tenchu2`):**\n46\t\n47\t- Dev folder: `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734/` (every dev file goes in here).\n48\t- Single-file game in the root: `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734.html`.\n49\t- `exit-interview.json` in the root, beside the HTML.\n50\t\n51\tIf your own TASK.md carries a different model or timestamp suffix, use yours. The title stays.\n52\t\n53\t---\n54\t\n55\t## 1. Title selection (done; do not change)\n56\t\n57\tTASK.md asks for a playful riff on the source's name, chosen by a real RNG from 50 silently brainstormed candidates.\n58\tThe 50 candidates were written into a script and one was drawn with Python's `secrets.randbelow(50)` (the OS CSPRNG).\n59\tThe draw was 26, so entry #27 won: **\"Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins\"**. It riffs on *Tenchu 2: Birth of\n60\tthe Stealth Assassins* (Tenchu → Bentou/bento; Stealth → Lunchbox). The world and story build on it: the \"2\" is the\n61\ttwo-tier box and the two apprentices. The title screen shows **BENTOU 2** in large type with the subtitle *Birth of the\n62\tLunchbox Assassins*.\n63\t\n64\t---\n65\t\n66\t## 2. What makes the source distinctive, and how this game captures it\n67\t\n68\tFacts about the source come from research (Wikipedia's article on the game; see the Source Information in section 10).\n69\tTenchu 2 (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000) is a prequel to the first Tenchu. Three Azuma clan ninja (two\n70\tcampaigns) support a young lord against a coup in Sengoku Japan. Compared with the first game, it adds:\n71\t\n72\t- redesigned swimming;\n73\t- more stealth kills;\n74\t- guards that hear better and call reinforcements;\n75\t- escort missions;\n76\t- ranks per mission that unlock gadgets;\n77\t- a widely praised Mission Editor.\n78\t\n79\tIts signatures, and our *original* version of each (no names, characters, levels, music or art are taken from it):\n80\t\n81\t| Source signature | Our version |\n82\t|---|---|\n83\t| Stealth first; detection is dangerous; the camera limits what you see | **Shadow Sight** hides enemies the ninja cannot see. **Light and shadow, noise and cover** decide detection. Being seen brings shouts, the alarm bell and reinforcements |\n84\t| Ki meter: a number showing how near enemies are, colored by their awareness | **Ki Gauge** (bottom left): 0–99 for the nearest sensed enemy; teal, yellow, orange or red with `?` or `!`; a taiko heartbeat when high. **Ki Focus** (hold L2/Tab) extends the sense |\n85\t| Instant cinematic stealth kills with an on-screen kanji splash | **Silent Cuts**: 5 directions (back, side, unaware front, from above, from the water), different for each character, with slow motion, a zoom and a red brush splash of **静斬** (\"silent cut\", an original choice; not the source's kanji) |\n86\t| Grappling hook to rooftops | **Kaginawa**: the only way onto roofs. Auto-target, an aim mode, and mouse targeting |\n87\t| Ninja tools carried into missions; items chosen before each mission | **The Bento**: 8 compartments (2 tiers × 4) packed on a \"Pack the Bento\" screen. Food tools (rice balls, poisoned rice, sleep dango, sour plum) and steel tools (shuriken, smoke, caltrops, firecracker, fire pot, straw cloak) |\n88\t| Poisoned rice that guards eat | The **Poison Rice Ball**, the game's signature lunchbox item; hungry guards complain about garrison rice |\n89\t| Ranks after each mission from kills and times spotted; high ranks unlock gadgets | Results scroll with a hanko rank stamp: **Grand Kaiseki / Makunouchi / Ekiben / Hinomaru / Leftovers** (bento grades). High ranks unlock tools |\n90\t| Lord's briefing, mission, boss at the end | Briefings in the shop or the lord's garden; every mission ends in a boss duel |\n91\t| Tenchu 2: swimming; enemies call reinforcements; escort missions | Moats and lakes to swim and dive (unseen, with a breath limit); Undertow kills; an alarm bell; the escort of the courier Tobei |\n92\t| Tenchu 2: Mission Editor | **Workshop**: a full controller-friendly editor on the same level format the campaign uses; save, test, play, export JSON |\n93\t| Several playable ninja, one story | Sojiro and Kaede. Same missions, different stats, moves, Silent Cuts and lines |\n94\t| Tone: earnest, melodramatic feudal drama, stoic ninja, a traitor, a hint of the supernatural, comic guard chatter | Same register: a starving province, a corrupt magistrate, a traitor chamberlain in a cursed oni mask, a rival ninja band, guards who mutter about bad rice |\n95\t\n96\t---\n97\t\n98\t## 3. Technology and architecture\n99\t\n100\t### 3.1 Stack and folder layout\n101\t\n102\t- **Engine:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff package (`github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`), the full\n103\t  readable engine `my-3d2dge.js` (one file, no dependencies). Read its `API.md` whole, `kits/stealth.js` whole (it\n104\t  already has guards with `E.sees` / `E.Suspicion`, FlowField chasing, takedowns, parry, Shell HUD, layered music) and\n105\t  `docs/ASSETS.md` whole. Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names. The game starts from the STEALTH kit's slice, reorganized into\n106\t  the modules below (copy its patterns; delete the kit's starter shell, title menu and other slices).\n107\t- **Multiplayer:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client `session.js` 1.4.0, pasted unmodified\n108\t  (`raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`). The harness (`harness.html`, `bridge.js`,\n109\t  `round.js`) is for tests only.\n110\t- **Tooling:** Node 20+ (the machine has Node 24), Playwright with Chromium (the handoff's `package.json` pins it) for\n111\t  the browser checks, and Python's `http.server` only for the hub harness.\n112\t- **No other libraries, no external fonts, no image or audio files.** Everything is drawn and synthesized in code.\n113\t\n114\t```text\n115\t<root>/                                        (the folder holding TASK.md and this PLAN.md)\n116\t  Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734.html   final single file (built)\n117\t  exit-interview.json\n118\t  Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734/       dev folder\n119\t    engine/my-3d2dge.js        copy of the handoff engine, patched (section 3.3); engine/PATCHES.md lists every change\n120\t    vendor/aihub/session.js    unmodified client; harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (tests only)\n121\t    handoff/                   API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, docs/ASSETS.md, kits/stealth.js, tools/*.mjs (check,\n122\t                               filmstrip, replay, asset-sheet, asset-find), package.json: reference + tools\n123\t    src/                       the game, in load order (section 3.4)\n124\t    index.html                 dev page: loads engine + each src file with <script> tags (works from file://)\n125\t    tools/build.mjs            bundles into the single HTML in <root>\n126\t    tests/run.mjs              THE test command (section 9) + tests/*.test.mjs + tests/browser/*.mjs\n127\t    shots/                     screenshots and filmstrips (output)\n128\t```\n129\t\n130\tEnvironment rules (from TASK.md):\n131\t\n132\t- Read nothing outside your folder that you don't need; other agents share this machine.\n133\t- Prefer `file://` and headless tools.\n134\t- The hub harness needs a server. Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from the folder being served, parse\n135\t  the port it prints, and confirm the served page is your game before trusting a result.\n136\t- Stop only the processes you started, by PID. Never use `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n137\t- `/tmp` on this machine is a small, nearly full tmpfs. Keep temp files inside the dev folder.\n138\t\n139\t### 3.2 Build and bundle (`tools/build.mjs`)\n140\t\n141\tOne command, `node tools/build.mjs`, writes `<root>/Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734.html`:\n142\t\n143\t```html\n144\t<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n145\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n146\t<script>/* session.js, byte-for-byte unmodified (starts with \"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0\") */</script>\n147\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n148\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n149\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n150\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n151\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n152\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Silent kills, unseen, fast: top ninja score wins\">\n153\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move WASD/stick · Strike click/□ · Jump Space/✕ · Crouch C/○ · Tool R/R2\">\n154\t<title>Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins</title>\n155\t<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n156\t</head><body>\n157\t<!-- E.bootSplash('BENTOU 2') markup -->\n158\t<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n159\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js (patched) */</script>\n160\t<script>/* the game: src/*.js concatenated, in order, inside ONE IIFE: (() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge; ... })(); */</script>\n161\t</body></html>\n162\t```\n163\t\n164\t- Escape every `</script` inside the inlined code as `<\\/script`.\n165\t- The session client must be the **first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`**, unmodified.\n166\t- The goal meta is at most 60 characters and the howto meta at most 80.\n167\t- `tools/build.mjs --js` writes only the concatenated game script to `dev/build/game.js`. The tests load that, so tests\n168\t  and the bundle run the same code.\n169\t- The build fails loudly if a `src` file is missing from the order list or if `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|lorem` appears in\n170\t  `src`.\n171\t\n172\t### 3.3 Engine patches (do them in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, mark each `// BENTOU PATCH n`, list them in `PATCHES.md` and on the About screen)\n173\t\n174\t1. **Pixel font glyphs.** Add `✕ ○ □ △` to the 5×7 font `G57` (7-row bitmaps), so `input.label()` text (which returns\n175\t   them for PlayStation pads) renders in canvas text and dialogs instead of `?`.\n176\t2. **Button symbols setting.** In `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs`, make the default `'playstation'` and the options\n177\t   `[['playstation','PlayStation'],['xbox','Xbox']]`. TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs, with an option for Xbox A B X Y.\n178\t3. **Humanoid gear** (in the head and weapon draw code, around the face block that draws eyes and mouth):\n179\t   - `mask: { color, style: 'cloth' | 'oni' }`. Cloth covers nose and mouth and keeps the eyes; it skips the mouth and\n180\t     also draws in portraits. Oni draws a red face with tusks, heavy brows and glowing eyes.\n181\t   - New hats: `hat: 'jingasa'` (wide shallow cone) and `hat: 'kabuto'` (helmet with a crest; `crest` color).\n182\t   - New weapons:\n183\t     - `weapon: 'spear'` (yari: a staff with a blade tip);\n184\t     - `weapon: 'bow'` (a curved stave with a string to the draw hand; drawn while `point` is true);\n185\t     - `weapon: 'club'` (kanabo: thick, tapered, studded).\n186\t   - `offhand: { len }`: a second short blade in the left hand (twin kodachi, twin kama).\n187\t   - `sashimono: color`: a small back banner on a pole (samurai).\n188\t\n189\t   Check each with `node handoff/tools/filmstrip.mjs` and the Animation Lab views.\n190\t4. **Shell: custom rows.** In `Shell._render`, add `if (s.rows) for (const k of v(s.rows)) add(this._row(k));`, so a\n191\t   custom screen can show settings rows (sliders, toggles, choices). In `_settingsRows`, skip the group `'Dev'`, so dev\n192\t   sliders never appear in the player's Settings.\n193\t5. **Shell: hover moves focus.** Add a `pointermove` listener on the screen that focuses the focusable under the\n194\t   pointer (`preventScroll: true`). TASK.md requires that hover moves the focus.\n195\t6. **Shell: 10-foot scale.** Add a CSS variable `--ui` (default\n196\t   `clamp(1, (innerHeight/720) * userScale, 3)`) and apply it with `zoom: var(--ui)` on `.esh-mod`, `.esh-ttl>div`,\n197\t   `.esh-toast`, `.esh-pr`, `.esh-tut`. Recompute it on resize. `userScale` comes from the setting \"Interface size\"\n198\t   (Normal 1, Large 1.25, Huge 1.5). Raise the base font to 16 px and buttons to a minimum height of 52 px.\n199\t7. **Music track envelopes.** In `_note`, honor per-track `pluck: true` (non-held exponential decay over\n200\t   `ring`, default 1.1 s), `attack` (default .006) and `release`. Koto, shamisen and harp plucks then ring and decay.\n201\t   Shakuhachi uses a slow attack (.09) with `vib`.\n202\t8. **Voice bus.** Expose `audio.voiceBus` (a gain on `_master`, created in `_init`), and apply the game setting\n203\t   `voices` (0–1) to it. The voice synth (section 5.17) connects there.\n204\t9. **Hub pause guard.** While `window.AIHub && AIHub.active` and `Pad8` (Create) is held, ignore the `pause` action\n205\t   (Options). The hub owns Create + Options.\n206\t\n207\tKeep every patch small, and don't refactor the engine.\n208\t\n209\t### 3.4 Module map (`src/`, concatenated in this order inside one IIFE)\n210\t\n211\t| File | Responsibility | Key exports (on the shared `B` namespace object) |\n212\t|---|---|---|\n213\t| `00-core.js` | namespace `B`, registries `B.def(kind, id, spec)` / `B.get(kind, id)` / `B.all(kind)`, event bus `B.on/off/emit`, `rand()` (gameplay, Math.random) vs `crand` (cosmetic E.rng stream), math helpers | `B`, `def`, `bus` |\n214\t| `01-tune.js` | every balance number as a `game.settings` entry in group `'Dev'` (section 5.20 table), `B.T(key)` getter with difficulty multipliers | `TUNE`, `T()` |\n215\t| `02-input.js` | action map (section 4.1), wheel listener, `B.intentFromInput()` (stick + keys, d-pad excluded in play), device and touch-only detection, \"any input\" clock for attract | `PlayerInput` |\n216\t| `03-glyphs.js` | pixel button icons per device and family; `B.glyph(g, action, x, y, o)`, and inline `{a:jump}` tokens in canvas text | `Glyph` |\n217\t| `04-camera.js` | follow, 45-degree rotation, zoom, look-ahead (mouse lean, Focus + right stick), cinematic overrides (Silent Cut zoom, boss intro, cutscenes) | `Cam` |\n218\t| `10-audio.js` | `audio.define` sfx set, songs with layers (section 5.17), `B.music.mood(level)` | `Sfx`, `Songs`, `Music` |\n219\t| `11-voice.js` | gibberish formant voice synth, speaker profiles, dialog hook, barks with distance and panning | `Voice` |\n220\t| `20-assets.js` | `E.SHAPES` / `E.MATERIALS` / `E.PATTERNS` for Japanese props, floor textures, wall `decorate` functions, the kawara roof-cap renderer, string sprites (item icons, crest, kanji, moon, eyes) | `Art` |\n221\t| `21-rigs.js` | character factories (section 6.1), `Hound` quadruped class, joint post-processing helpers (arms-back ninja run, wall-hug pose, eating, sleeping, mouth cover) | `Rigs`, `Hound` |\n222\t| `30-world.js` | level JSON → `World` (TileMap + navigation map + light map + hide map + water + anchors + props + lights + zones); queries (`lightAt`, `isHide`, `isDeep`, `anchorsNear`, `nearestBell`, `zoneAt`) | `World` |\n223\t| `31-actors.js` | base `Actor` (a Mover plus rig plus HP plus status); spawn helpers | `Actor` |\n224\t| `40-hero.js` | hero controller from an *intent* (section 5.1): traversal, swim, hug, drag, focus, noise emission, tool use, combat hooks | `Hero` |\n225\t| `41-silentcut.js` | Silent Cut detection and `E.ACTIONS` entries per variant and character; cinematic and splash | `SilentCut` |\n226\t| `42-grapple.js` | anchor search, targeting UI, `E.ACTIONS.grapple`, rope drawing | `Grapple` |\n227\t| `43-combat.js` | damage pipeline (`B.damage(src, dst, amount, kind)`), hero combos and jump attack, block, parry, riposte, dodge, i-frames, hit fx | `Combat` |\n228\t| `44-tools.js` | the 10 tools: data and behavior (projectiles, lobs, clouds, traps, baits), `Bento` loadout model | `Tools`, `Bento` |\n229\t| `50-perception.js` | sight (exposure from light, crouch, cover, motion, look-up limit, smoke), hearing (`B.noise(x,y,z,loud,kind)`), smell, body discovery, Shadow Sight visibility, Ki values | `Perception` |\n230\t| `51-guard-brain.js` | guard state machine on top of `E.Suspicion` (section 5.4), patrol, post, sleep, eat, chat, search, chase, fight, flee, bark scheduling, alarm and bell logic | `Brain` |\n231\t| `52-enemies.js` | archetype registry: ashigaru, samurai, archer, ninja, hound, civilians, disguised | `def('enemy',...)` |\n232\t| `53-bosses.js` | `Boss` base with phases and pattern scripts (`game.script` generators); Ittetsu, Gonroku, Hotaru, Kurogane | `def('boss',...)` |\n233\t| `54-escort.js` | the escort follower (Tobei) | `Escort` |\n234\t| `60-mission.js` | mission runtime: objectives, triggers, timers, checkpoints, fail states, pickups, interactions | `Mission` |\n235\t| `61-score.js` | scoring events → score, ranks, unlocks, best records, results data | `Score` |\n236\t| `62-story.js` | all text: crawl, briefings, cutscene scripts, boss lines, barks, results comments (section 6.6) | `Story` |\n237\t| `63-cutscene.js` | cutscene player (staged rigs, camera tweens, letterbox, `E.Dialog` with portraits and voices, skip) | `Cutscene` |\n238\t| `64-levels-*.js` | one file per level: training, m1, m2, m3, delivery (data only, `def('level', id, {...})`) | level data |\n239\t| `65-missions.js` | mission metadata (`def('mission', id, {...})`): title, level, briefing, loadout hint, par, unlock rules, next | mission data |\n240\t| `70-hud.js` | canvas HUD (section 4.4): health, Ki gauge, tool box, prompts, tutorial cards, toasts, boss bar, timer, breath, stamina, awareness marks, threat arrows, letterbox, splash | `Hud` |\n241\t| `71-scenes-menu.js` | boot, title (idle timer), main menu, character select, mission select, about/credits, touch-only notice | scenes |\n242\t| `72-scenes-story.js` | briefing, bento packing, results, game over, ending and credits | scenes |\n243\t| `73-scene-mission.js` | the gameplay scene used by story, trial, hub, attract and workshop test play | `MissionScene` |\n244\t| `74-dev.js` | dev mode screens, cheats, overlays, sliders (section 5.20) | `Dev` |\n245\t| `75-workshop.js` | the Mission Editor (section 5.21) | scene `workshop` |\n246\t| `80-autopilot.js` | intent-producing autopilot (beats), shared by attract mode and the playthrough test; per-mission routes | `Autopilot` |\n247\t| `81-attract.js` | attract director and vignettes (section 5.19) | scene `attract` |\n248\t| `82-hub.js` | AI Hub ghost mode, own card, ghost send and draw, progress and result, end handling; Shadow Trial ghost recording | `Hub`, scene `hubCard` |\n249\t| `90-main.js` | `new E.Game(...)`, scene registration, boot steps, saves wiring, `game.debug`, `window.__BENTOU` | — |\n250\t\n251\tArchitecture rules (the Emberdeep lessons from AI_GUIDE):\n252\t\n253\t- **A spine, then content.** Content (levels, enemies, tools, bosses, lines) is data in registries and never edits the\n254\t  core. Systems talk through the **event bus**:\n255\t\n256\t  ```text\n257\t  noise, seen, detected, alert, bodyFound, silentCut, kill, damage, heroDeath, toolUsed,\n258\t  objective, checkpoint, bell, boss, missionEnd\n259\t  ```\n260\t\n261\t  Score, HUD toasts, music mood, barks, hub progress and tests all listen. None of them is called directly from the\n262\t  combat or AI code.\n263\t- **One intent interface for the hero.** The player's input adapter, the autopilot and the tests all produce the same\n264\t  intent object (section 5.1), so attract mode never touches `game.input` and can't be mistaken for player input.\n265\t- **Game logic in world units, with `dt` everywhere.** Gameplay randomness uses `rand()` in update only; cosmetic\n266\t  randomness in draw uses `crand` (an `E.rng` stream). Draw code never consumes `Math.random`, which keeps hub-seeded\n267\t  runs and tests deterministic at any refresh rate.\n268\t- **No DOM at load in headless.** Guard every `matchMedia`, `document` and `navigator` use, so the game runs under\n269\t  `node:vm` (as `game/test.mjs` does).\n270\t\n271\t### 3.5 Scenes and flow\n272\t\n273\t```text\n274\tboot ─┬─(AIHub.active)──► hubCard ──start──► mission(mode:'hub') ──end──► hub results overlay\n275\t      └─► title ◄──────── any input ──── attract (after 10 s idle on title or main menu)\n276\t           │ menu: Continue · New Story · Missions · Shadow Trial · Workshop · Settings · About\n277\t           ├─ New Story ─► charSelect ─► story(crawl+prologue) ─► briefing ─► bento ─► mission ─► results ─► story ─► …\n278\t           │                                                     (training → m1 → m2 → m3 → ending+credits → title)\n279\t           ├─ Missions ─► missionSelect (character + mission, best ranks) ─► briefing ─► bento ─► mission ─► results\n280\t           ├─ Shadow Trial ─► bento(trial rules) ─► mission(mode:'trial', with your best ghost) ─► results(trial board)\n281\t           ├─ Workshop ─► workshop ◄─► mission(mode:'workshop')\n282\t           └─ About ─► about (pages)\n283\tmission: pausable. Pause = Shell pause: Resume · Restart from checkpoint · Restart mission · Objectives · Dev Mode ·\n284\t         Settings · Controls · Full screen · Quit to title   (hub: Resume · Settings · Controls only)\n285\tmission death ─► \"Your box is empty\" overlay: Retry from checkpoint · Restart mission · Quit\n286\t```\n287\t\n288\tScene options:\n289\t\n290\t- `mission`:\n291\t\n292\t  ```js\n293\t  { pausable: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'], res: 'ps1', expand: true, input: B.INPUT,\n294\t    touch: [], camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1.15, tall: 1.35, rotate: true, wheel: false } }\n295\t  ```\n296\t\n297\t- Menu scenes use the same input preset and `touch: []`.\n298\t- The title is a side-view diorama (`view: 'side'`) with a `PlatformMap` ledge and an `E.Backdrop`.\n299\t\n300\t### 3.6 Data formats (the campaign and the Workshop share them exactly)\n301\t\n302\t**Level** (`def('level', id, spec)`; the Workshop exports the same JSON):\n303\t\n304\t```js\n305\t{ id: 'm1', name: 'Rice and Ash', size: [56, 48], time: 'night' /* dusk | night | rain | festival */, ambient: .38,\n306\t  rows: ['########…', …],                 // terrain only, default legend below (48 strings of 56 chars)\n307\t  zones: [{ id: 'mansion', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], name: 'Kanemori Mansion' }],   // HUD place names\n308\t  lights: [{ at: [cx, cy], z: 18, r: 64, i: .9, color: '#ffb060', kind: 'stoneLantern' }],   // kind also places its prop\n309\t  props: [['stoneLantern', cx, cy, { facing: 0 }], ['bamboo', cx, cy], …],   // solid unless { solid: false }\n310\t  anchors: [[cx, cy, z]],                // extra grapple anchors (tree crowns, beams); roof edges are found automatically\n311\t  hero: { at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 0 }, exit: { at: [cx, cy], r: 1.5 },\n312\t  guards: [{ id: 'g1', type: 'ashigaru', at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 90, mode: 'patrol', lantern: true,\n313\t             route: [[cx, cy, wait, lookDeg], …], loop: true, partner: null, faction: 'kanemori' }],\n314\t  civilians: [{ id: 'c1', type: 'maid', at: [cx, cy], mode: 'idle', route: null, disguised: false }],\n315\t  pickups: [{ id: 'ledger', kind: 'story', at: [cx, cy], z: 0 }, { kind: 'tool', tool: 'riceball', n: 2, at: [cx, cy] }],\n316\t  bells: [[cx, cy]], barracks: [[cx, cy]],          // alarm bell spots; where reinforcements come out\n317\t  interact: [{ id: 'lever', at: [cx, cy], hold: 1.2, text: 'Open the water gate', do: [['open', cx, cy, w, h]] }],\n318\t  escort: { id: 'tobei', at: [cx, cy], hp: 60 },\n319\t  boss: { id: 'gonroku', at: [cx, cy], arena: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], start: 'trigger:court' },\n320\t  objectives: [{ id: 'kill', type: 'assassinate', target: 'kanemori', text: 'Silence Magistrate Kanemori' },\n321\t               { id: 'letter', type: 'retrieve', pickup: 'ledger', optional: true, text: 'Find what he hides' },\n322\t               { id: 'escape', type: 'reach', exit: true, after: ['kill', 'boss'], text: 'Escape by the canal boat' }],\n323\t  triggers: [{ id: 'court', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], once: true,\n324\t               do: [['checkpoint'], ['boss', 'gonroku'], ['say', 'gonroku', 'gon_intro']] }],\n325\t  timer: null,            // { seconds: 720, fail: 'text', stopOn: 'objective:sake' }\n326\t  par: 600, music: 'm1', weather: null }\n327\t```\n328\t\n329\tTrigger conditions:\n330\t\n331\t- `rect` / `at+r` (enter);\n332\t- `when: 'objective:<id>'`;\n333\t- `'kill:<id>'`;\n334\t- `'alert'`;\n335\t- `'time:<s>'`;\n336\t- `'pickup:<id>'`.\n337\t\n338\tTrigger actions:\n339\t\n340\t- `say`, `toast`, `tutorial`;\n341\t- `checkpoint`;\n342\t- `spawn` (a guard spec);\n343\t- `boss`, `cutscene`;\n344\t- `objective` (`show` | `done` | `fail`);\n345\t- `open` / `close` (`map.set` cells);\n346\t- `music` (layer);\n347\t- `flag`.\n348\t\n349\t**Default legend** (rows are terrain; actors are listed in the entity arrays):\n350\t\n351\t| Char | What | Rule |\n352\t|---|---|---|\n353\t| `.` | earth path | normal footsteps |\n354\t| `,` | tall grass | hide: crouched exposure ×0.15, standing ×0.6 |\n355\t| `\"` | bamboo grove | hide like grass; bamboo props scattered automatically (seeded by cell) |\n356\t| `:` | raked gravel | noise ×1.6; even crouch-walking makes noise 12 |\n357\t| `=` | wooden boards (engawa, pier) | noise ×1.2 when running; creak sfx |\n358\t| `_` | tatami (inside halls) | noise ×0.6 |\n359\t| `+` | stone paving | normal |\n360\t| `~` | deep water | swim/dive; guards and hounds never enter (nav map blocks it) |\n361\t| `-` | shallow water | wade: speed ×0.7, splash noise 40 even walking, no hiding |\n362\t| `#` | castle / outer stone wall (ishigaki) | h 56, face granite stone, top slab, `cut: true, cutH: 8`; grapple only |\n363\t| `W` | compound wall, plaster with tile cap | h 30 (climbable ledge), face plaster, roof tiles, `cut: true, cutH: 6` |\n364\t| `F` | bamboo fence | h 14 (vaulted at a run) |\n365\t| `H` | hall wall (enterable building perimeter) | h 40, face timber with shoji `decorate`, `cut: true, cutH: 6`; its roof cap is visual (section 5.18) |\n366\t| `d` | doorway in a hall wall | floor `door`; drawn as an open sliding door |\n367\t| `A` | townhouse (machiya) | h 40, plaster and timber with lattice, kawara roof (walkable) |\n368\t| `B` | two-story house or inn | h 64, timber and plaster, balcony, kawara roof |\n369\t| `C` | storehouse (kura) | h 48, white plaster with a namako band, heavy kawara roof |\n370\t| `D` | shop with noren curtain | h 40, timber, noren `decorate`, kawara roof |\n371\t| `S` | shrine or temple hall | h 56, vermilion pillars, dark kawara roof |\n372\t| `T` | watchtower (yagura), 2×2 | h 80, plank, small roof; archers stand on top |\n373\t| `G` / `K` / `M` | castle keep tiers | h 64 / 112 / 160; ishigaki base to z 24, then white plaster; chidori gables; golden shachihoko on `M` |\n374\t| `P` | planter or stone platform | h 10 (jump up; cover when crouched behind it) |\n375\t| `R` | rocks | h 20, face rock, climbable |\n376\t\n377\tEvery solid building has a flat walkable top at its height. \"No passages under things\" is an engine rule, so halls are\n378\tenterable but their roofs are not walkable.\n379\t\n380\t**Guard / enemy archetype** (`def('enemy', id, spec)`):\n381\t\n382\t```js\n383\t{ rig, hp, walk, run, sight: { range, fov, lookUp }, hear, smell, moves: [...], ranged, climbs, faction, barks,\n384\t  canSilentCut: true }\n385\t```\n386\t\n387\t**Tool** (`def('tool', id, spec)`):\n388\t\n389\t```js\n390\t{ name, icon, stack, use: 'eat' | 'throw' | 'lob' | 'drop' | 'self', range, effect(ctx), unlock }\n391\t```\n392\t\n393\t**Mission** (`def('mission', id, spec)`):\n394\t\n395\t```js\n396\t{ title, level, briefing, debrief, loadoutHint: [...], par, next, unlocks: [{ tool, rank }] }\n397\t```\n398\t\n399\t---\n400\t\n401\t## 4. Controls and UX: controller first, 10 feet from a TV\n402\t\n403\t### 4.1 Action map (`B.INPUT`, passed as `new E.Game({ input })`; every action is rebindable on the standard Controls screen)\n404\t\n405\t| Action | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (Settings) | Keyboard + mouse | Notes |\n406\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n407\t| Move | Left stick (tilt <55% = quiet walk) | Left stick | WASD / arrows | in play the d-pad does **not** move: the hero reads the stick and keys only |\n408\t| Camera | Right stick: ←/→ flick turns 45°, ↑/↓ zooms | Right stick | Q / E turn 45°, − / = zoom; mouse leans the view toward the cursor | R3 / X resets the camera |\n409\t| Jump · climb · vault | ✕ (Pad0) | A | Space | parkour first (ledge ≤ 30, vault ≤ 14, gap leap) |\n410\t| Crouch (toggle; hold in Settings) | ○ (Pad1) | B | C | **never bind Ctrl**: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab |\n411\t| Strike · Silent Cut · riposte | □ (Pad2) | X | Left click / J | context: the prompt says which |\n412\t| Interact (drag body, pick up, open, talk, lever) | △ (Pad3) | Y | F (or left click on a highlighted thing) | |\n413\t| Block (hold) · parry (timed) | L1 (Pad4) | LB | Right click / K | block + jump + direction = dodge roll |\n414\t| Grappling hook (tap: fire at the highlighted anchor; hold: aim) | R1 (Pad5) | RB | G / middle click | with the mouse: the anchor under the cursor |\n415\t| Ki Focus (hold) | L2 (Pad6) | LT | Tab | slows to a walk; sense radius 220; right stick or mouse scouts further |\n416\t| Use tool | R2 (Pad7) | RT | R | thrown at the cursor (mouse) or auto-aimed (pad/keys) |\n417\t| Sprint | L3 (Pad10, a toggle until the stick is released) | LS | Shift (hold) | stamina |\n418\t| Previous / next tool | D-pad ← / → | D-pad | mouse wheel, 1–8 picks a compartment | |\n419\t| Eat a rice ball (quick heal) | D-pad ↓ | D-pad ↓ | H | |\n420\t| Whistle (lure) | D-pad ↑ | D-pad ↑ | V | noise 70 at the hero: lures nearby guards to search |\n421\t| Objectives | Create (Pad8) | View | M | shows the objectives panel (in a hub session Create does nothing: the hub owns Create + Options) |\n422\t| Pause | Options (Pad9) | Menu | Esc / P | engine standard (hub: ignored while Create is held) |\n423\t| Menus | d-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | A / B | arrows, Enter, Esc; mouse hover focuses, click picks | |\n424\t\n425\tImplementation notes:\n426\t\n427\t- Action names, in `B.INPUT` and on the Controls screen (`menu.controls` gives the names):\n428\t\n429\t  | Action | Controls name |\n430\t  |---|---|\n431\t  | `jump` | Jump / climb |\n432\t  | `crouch` | Crouch |\n433\t  | `attack` | Strike / Silent Cut |\n434\t  | `interact` | Interact |\n435\t  | `block` | Block / parry |\n436\t  | `grapple` | Grappling hook |\n437\t  | `focus` | Ki Focus |\n438\t  | `useTool` | Use tool |\n439\t  | `sprint` | Sprint |\n440\t  | `toolPrev` | Previous tool |\n441\t  | `toolNext` | Next tool |\n442\t  | `heal` | Eat rice ball |\n443\t  | `lure` | Whistle |\n444\t  | `camLeft` | Turn camera left |\n445\t  | `camRight` | Turn camera right |\n446\t  | `camReset` | Reset camera |\n447\t  | `objectives` | Objectives |\n448\t\n449\t  The engine adds `up/down/left/right/start/pause/confirm/cancel`. Its menu actions `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z,\n450\t  pad A) and `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B) overlap some play keys; that is harmless, because play never\n451\t  reads them.\n452\t- Movement in play is `B.intentFromInput()`: the left stick from `input.padAxes` with the radial deadzone, plus the\n453\t  key codes of the `up/down/left/right` actions that are not `Pad*`, through `game.view.screenDirToGround`. Menus still\n454\t  use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the d-pad.\n455\t- Tool cycling with the wheel: set `camera.wheel: false` on the mission scene and add a passive `wheel` listener that\n456\t  taps `toolPrev` / `toolNext`.\n457\t- `input.lastDevice` decides prompts. A mouse used in the last 3 s means \"mouse mode\": cursor aiming, hover highlights\n458\t  and camera lean. A stick or key press ends it.\n459\t- Mouse in the world:\n460\t  - Hovering a guard shows its awareness meter and type label.\n461\t  - Hovering a highlighted interactable within reach changes the left click from Strike to Interact.\n462\t  - Hovering a valid roof edge or anchor highlights it for G / middle click.\n463\t  - Strikes face the cursor (Diablo-style).\n464\t  - Thrown tools land at `game.mouseGround()`, clamped to range.\n465\t\n466\t### 4.2 Glyphs and prompts (`03-glyphs.js`)\n467\t\n468\t- Every prompt, tutorial card, menu footer and dialog token follows the last device used, and redraws the moment it\n469\t  changes.\n470\t- **Pad (PlayStation):** a dark circle with a colored symbol: ✕ blue `#7ab4ff`, ○ red `#ff6a6a`, □ pink `#ff8ad8`,\n471\t  △ green `#5ae0a0`.\n472\t- **Pad (Xbox):** A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow.\n473\t- **Shoulders, triggers and buttons:** L1/R1/L2/R2 (LB/RB/LT/RT) are rounded tabs. Sticks are rings with an arrow.\n474\t  The d-pad is a cross with the used arm lit. Create/Options (View/Menu) are pills.\n475\t- **Keyboard:** a light keycap with `input.codeLabel(code)`.\n476\t- **Mouse:** a mouse icon with the left, right or middle button lit, or the wheel.\n477\t- Icons are 9–11 game pixels tall and drawn with `E.px` (no font dependency). Canvas text can embed `{a:attack}`,\n478\t  which renders that action's icon inline.\n479\t- HTML (Shell) text uses `input.label()` (Unicode is fine there).\n480\t\n481\t### 4.3 Screens (big, sparse, one decision per screen; never dense web-style tables)\n482\t\n483\tCanvas screens use `E.Menu`, which already moves its cursor on hover and picks on click. HTML screens (pause, settings,\n484\tcontrols, dev, objectives, Workshop menus, About) use one `E.Shell` with this theme:\n485\t\n486\t```js\n487\t{ ink: '#f4ead5', paper: 'rgba(20,12,12,.92)', accent: '#e8b04a', muted: '#b8a890', danger: '#d8402a',\n488\t  line: 'rgba(232,176,74,.35)', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: 'Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' }\n489\t```\n490\t\n491\t- **Title** (canvas, side view):\n492\t  - A night sky with a big moon over a castle silhouette (custom `E.Backdrop`: moon, stars, mountains, castle, fog).\n493\t  - Sojiro and Kaede on a tiled ridge in front, scarves fluttering, cherry petals falling.\n494\t  - The logo is `E.font.title('BENTOU 2', … { scale: 4, colors: gold → vermilion, depth: 3 })` with the subtitle below\n495\t    and the clan crest stamp.\n496\t  - \"PRESS {a:start}\" first, then the `E.Menu`: Continue · New Story · Missions · Shadow Trial · Workshop · Settings\n497\t    (`game.menu('settings')`) · About. Missing items are hidden (no Continue without a save).\n498\t  - Version line: `E.versionLabel()` + game version, small, bottom right.\n499\t- **Character select:**\n500\t  - Two rigs on a rooftop, side by side; ←/→ or hover picks one.\n501\t  - Name, weapon, three short bars (Strength, Speed, Stealth) and one sentence.\n502\t  - A spoken gibberish greeting with a subtitle.\n503\t- **Mission select:** a vertical list of unlocked missions on a scroll. Each shows its best rank stamp per character\n504\t  and the character toggle (L1/R1).\n505\t- **Briefing:**\n506\t  - A painted interior (the shop's back room: shoji, stacked boxes, a lantern; or the lord's moonlit garden) with live\n507\t    portraits (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n508\t  - `E.Dialog` lines with names and voices, then an objectives card (2–3 lines).\n509\t  - Hold {a:start} to skip.\n510\t- **Pack the Bento:**\n511\t  - A black-lacquer two-tier box seen from above; each tier has 4 compartments.\n512\t  - The left column is the tool shelf (big icons, name, one-line effect). The stick moves, ✕ fills the focused\n513\t    compartment, ○ empties it, △ restores the mission's suggested loadout, Options starts.\n514\t  - Mouse: hover focuses, click places, right click empties.\n515\t  - Shows each stack count. The last loadout is remembered.\n516\t- **Results:**\n517\t  - A scroll unrolls. One stat line appears at a time with a brush underline: Time, Silent Cuts, Kills, Times detected,\n518\t    Civilians harmed, Optional tasks, Tools used, Retries. Then the score counts up.\n519\t  - The rank hanko slams down (screen thump, stamp sound).\n520\t  - Granny's one-line comment, and a \"New tool\" card if one unlocked.\n521\t  - Buttons: Continue · Retry · Missions.\n522\t- **Game over overlay:** time slows, the screen desaturates, \"YOUR BOX IS EMPTY\" in brush type, and three choices.\n523\t- **About / Credits:** paged (◀ ▶), one section per page, large type (section 5.23).\n524\t- **Ending:** cutscene, then a credits roll over the moon. Any input speeds it up; it returns to the title.\n525\t\n526\t### 4.4 In-game HUD (canvas, anchored to `r.W` / `r.H`, inside 4% overscan margins)\n527\t\n528\t| Where | Element |\n529\t|---|---|\n530\t| top left | health bar (brush stroke in vermilion, the character's crest at its head); below it **静斬 ×n** (Silent Cut count) |\n531\t| top center | objective toast on change (fades after 4 s); the boss bar (wide, the name in brush caps, phase ticks); \"ALARM!\" banner |\n532\t| top right | M3 moon timer (an arc with the moon's position; turns red under 60 s); place name on entering a zone (fades) |\n533\t| bottom left | **Ki Gauge**: an 18-px-radius semicircle with the number 0–99 in large digits (font scale 2), a colored ring and `?`/`!`; the eye icon in its middle shows your light (closed = shadow, half = dim, open = lit) |\n534\t| bottom right | **tool box**: the selected tool's icon (16 px at scale 2) with its count; neighbors slide by on change; d-pad glyphs |\n535\t| bottom center | context prompts (at most 2): icon + label (\"□ Silent Cut — Back\", \"R1 Grapple\", \"△ Drag body\", \"△ Hold: open gate\" with a progress ring) |\n536\t| over the hero | breath bubbles when diving; a stamina ring when <100 |\n537\t| over guards | `?` yellow (notice), `?` orange (search), `!` red (alert), `Zz` (asleep), `…` (eating), with a small suspicion bar; tinted by Shadow Sight state |\n538\t| screen edges | red chevrons toward alerted enemies off screen; `r.marker` objective diamond (Settings: Objective marker) |\n539\t| cinematic | letterbox bars (Silent Cuts, boss intros, cutscenes); the 静斬 splash; a red edge pulse when hit |\n540\t\n541\tThe objectives panel (Create/M) is an `E.Shell` screen: the mission title, objectives with checkmarks, the time, and\n542\tSilent Cuts so far. In the pause menu it is \"Objectives\".\n543\t\n544\t### 4.5 Touch-only devices\n545\t\n546\t- Detection: `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, with no gamepad connected\n547\t  and no key pressed yet.\n548\t- Then: `input.touchEnabled = false`, and no scene declares touch buttons.\n549\t- The title replaces its menu with a large panel: **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, a line (\"Connect a controller\n550\t  or a keyboard to play.\"), and a big **Settings** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). The engine corner menu button\n551\t  stays.\n552\t- Attract mode runs after 10 s as usual, and a tap returns to the title.\n553\t- `gamepadconnected` or any key press removes the notice at once.\n554\t\n555\t### 4.6 Settings (the engine's standard screens plus ours in group \"Game\"; Sound gets \"Voices\")\n556\t\n557\t| Setting | Values (default first) |\n558\t|---|---|\n559\t| Button symbols *(engine, patched)* | PlayStation · Xbox |\n560\t| Interface size | Auto · Normal · Large · Huge |\n561\t| Difficulty | Ninja · Novice · Grand Master: guard perception ×1 / .8 / 1.2, damage taken ×1 / .6 / 1.4, Ki range ×1 / 1.2 / .85 |\n562\t| Camera angle | Low (iso) · High (threequarter) |\n563\t| Invert camera turn | Off · On |\n564\t| Crouch | Toggle · Hold |\n565\t| Sight cones | On · Off (the faint cones of guards you can see) |\n566\t| Objective marker | On · Off |\n567\t| Show all enemies (assist) | Off · On (Shadow Sight off) |\n568\t| Ki heartbeat | On · Off |\n569\t| Text speed | Normal · Slow · Fast |\n570\t| Blood | Ink · Off (red ink splashes and decals) |\n571\t| Voices *(Sound)* | slider 0–1, default .8 |\n572\t\n573\t### 4.7 Camera\n574\t\n575\t- `game.follow(hero, { z: 18, lead: 10 })`, `cam.smooth = .12`, `cam.bounds = v => world.map.bounds(v)`.\n576\t- **Turn:** `game.rotateView(±45)` with a .25 s cooldown and a short whoosh. The compass on the tool box shows north.\n577\t  Movement stays screen-relative through `screenDirToGround`.\n578\t- **Zoom:** .75–2×, starting at 1.15 (1.35 on a tall screen). Right stick ↑/↓ or −/=.\n579\t- **Look-ahead:** mouse mode leans the focus toward the cursor by up to 40 units (140 with Focus). Pad: Focus + right\n580\t  stick pans up to 140 units, eased back on release.\n581\t- **Cinematics:**\n582\t  - Silent Cut: zoom tween to 1.8× in .15 s, `timeScale = T('slowmo')` for .55 s, letterbox, then restore.\n583\t  - Boss intro: a `game.tween` pan to the boss, the name card, then a pan back.\n584\t  - Cutscenes: scripted focus and zoom.\n585\t  - Respect Reduce motion: no shake, shorter zooms.\n586\t- **Occlusion:**\n587\t  - The hero always draws with `xray: { actors: true }`. Visible guards draw with `xray: { color: <awareness color> }`.\n588\t  - Walls nearest the camera use `cut`.\n589\t  - Hall roof caps fade while the hero is inside that hall (section 5.18).\n590\t\n591\t---\n592\t\n593\t## 5. Systems\n594\t\n595\tNumbers marked *T* are live dev sliders (section 5.20). Every system emits bus events and is covered by tests (section 9).\n596\t\n597\t### 5.1 Hero, intent and traversal (`40-hero.js`)\n598\t\n599\t**Intent** (built by `PlayerInput`, `Autopilot` or a test):\n600\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"0f57e53f-ffe5-45e1-964c-0e69634a7844","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:36.564Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183420__xf7f297/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins\n\n*An original isometric ninja stealth-action game, a playful riff on* Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins.\n*Build plan for the developers (human or AI) who will build it from TASK.md and this file alone.*\n\n---\n\n## 0. At a glance\n\n**Pitch.** Kasugai Province, the Sengoku era. The granaries are full and the people starve. In the shadow of Kokaku\nCastle, a humble shop, the **Jubako-ya**, sells two-tier lunchboxes (jubako) to the lord's household. Its boxes have two\ntiers. So does the shop: one tier for the rice and one for the blade. You play one of its two apprentices, **Sojiro**\n(katana, steady) or **Kaede** (twin short blades, quick), through the night they pass their trial and become true\n**Lunchbox Assassins**. The story is played straight, in the source's earnest, terse feudal-drama voice. The jokes are\ndeadpan and come from the world (poisoned rice balls, rank names taken from bento grades), never from winking.\n\n**Core loop (one sentence, put it at the top of the game code):** take a mission at the shop, pack your bento of ninja\ntools, slip into a lantern-lit night location unseen, silence guards with Silent Cuts, reach the target, survive the\nboss, escape, and earn a rank that unlocks new tools.\n\n**Genre:** third-person ninja stealth-action, with light melee combat and boss duels.\n**Perspective:** isometric third person on the engine's `iso` view (yaw 45, pitch 30), rotatable in 45-degree steps and\nzoomable, with `threequarter` as a Settings alternative (\"Camera angle: Low / High\"). Tenchu's behind-the-back 3D camera\nis not available in this 2D engine. Its job (limited sight, the ki sense, looking around corners) is rebuilt as\n**Shadow Sight** (section 5.5): enemies the ninja can't see are hidden unless the Ki gauge senses them.\n\n**Scope of the demo (all required, no stubs):**\n\n- A training mission and three story missions, each with a boss. That is about 45 minutes of play.\n- Two playable characters.\n- 10 tools, packed in the bento.\n- 5 guard types plus civilians and disguised enemies.\n- Silent Cuts from 5 directions.\n- Grappling hook, swimming and diving, body dragging, wall hugging, light and shadow, noise, alarm bells with\n  reinforcements, and an escort mission.\n- Ranks and unlocks, and saves.\n- Story cutscenes with gibberish voices.\n- Dev mode with live balance sliders.\n- An attract mode.\n- A Mission Editor (the \"Workshop\", after Tenchu 2's Mission Editor).\n- AI Hub ghost-mode multiplayer for 1–4 players, plus its standalone twin, the Shadow Trial, where you race your own\n  best ghost.\n- An About/Credits screen.\n\n**Deliverables (names follow TASK.md's bracket pattern with GameTitle = `Bentou2`, SOURCE = `Tenchu2`):**\n\n- Dev folder: `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734/` (every dev file goes in here).\n- Single-file game in the root: `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734.html`.\n- `exit-interview.json` in the root, beside the HTML.\n\nIf your own TASK.md carries a different model or timestamp suffix, use yours. The title stays.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Title selection (done; do not change)\n\nTASK.md asks for a playful riff on the source's name, chosen by a real RNG from 50 silently brainstormed candidates.\nThe 50 candidates were written into a script and one was drawn with Python's `secrets.randbelow(50)` (the OS CSPRNG).\nThe draw was 26, so entry #27 won: **\"Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins\"**. It riffs on *Tenchu 2: Birth of\nthe Stealth Assassins* (Tenchu → Bentou/bento; Stealth → Lunchbox). The world and story build on it: the \"2\" is the\ntwo-tier box and the two apprentices. The title screen shows **BENTOU 2** in large type with the subtitle *Birth of the\nLunchbox Assassins*.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What makes the source distinctive, and how this game captures it\n\nFacts about the source come from research (Wikipedia's article on the game; see the Source Information in section 10).\nTenchu 2 (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000) is a prequel to the first Tenchu. Three Azuma clan ninja (two\ncampaigns) support a young lord against a coup in Sengoku Japan. Compared with the first game, it adds:\n\n- redesigned swimming;\n- more stealth kills;\n- guards that hear better and call reinforcements;\n- escort missions;\n- ranks per mission that unlock gadgets;\n- a widely praised Mission Editor.\n\nIts signatures, and our *original* version of each (no names, characters, levels, music or art are taken from it):\n\n| Source signature | Our version |\n|---|---|\n| Stealth first; detection is dangerous; the camera limits what you see | **Shadow Sight** hides enemies the ninja cannot see. **Light and shadow, noise and cover** decide detection. Being seen brings shouts, the alarm bell and reinforcements |\n| Ki meter: a number showing how near enemies are, colored by their awareness | **Ki Gauge** (bottom left): 0–99 for the nearest sensed enemy; teal, yellow, orange or red with `?` or `!`; a taiko heartbeat when high. **Ki Focus** (hold L2/Tab) extends the sense |\n| Instant cinematic stealth kills with an on-screen kanji splash | **Silent Cuts**: 5 directions (back, side, unaware front, from above, from the water), different for each character, with slow motion, a zoom and a red brush splash of **静斬** (\"silent cut\", an original choice; not the source's kanji) |\n| Grappling hook to rooftops | **Kaginawa**: the only way onto roofs. Auto-target, an aim mode, and mouse targeting |\n| Ninja tools carried into missions; items chosen before each mission | **The Bento**: 8 compartments (2 tiers × 4) packed on a \"Pack the Bento\" screen. Food tools (rice balls, poisoned rice, sleep dango, sour plum) and steel tools (shuriken, smoke, caltrops, firecracker, fire pot, straw cloak) |\n| Poisoned rice that guards eat | The **Poison Rice Ball**, the game's signature lunchbox item; hungry guards complain about garrison rice |\n| Ranks after each mission from kills and times spotted; high ranks unlock gadgets | Results scroll with a hanko rank stamp: **Grand Kaiseki / Makunouchi / Ekiben / Hinomaru / Leftovers** (bento grades). High ranks unlock tools |\n| Lord's briefing, mission, boss at the end | Briefings in the shop or the lord's garden; every mission ends in a boss duel |\n| Tenchu 2: swimming; enemies call reinforcements; escort missions | Moats and lakes to swim and dive (unseen, with a breath limit); Undertow kills; an alarm bell; the escort of the courier Tobei |\n| Tenchu 2: Mission Editor | **Workshop**: a full controller-friendly editor on the same level format the campaign uses; save, test, play, export JSON |\n| Several playable ninja, one story | Sojiro and Kaede. Same missions, different stats, moves, Silent Cuts and lines |\n| Tone: earnest, melodramatic feudal drama, stoic ninja, a traitor, a hint of the supernatural, comic guard chatter | Same register: a starving province, a corrupt magistrate, a traitor chamberlain in a cursed oni mask, a rival ninja band, guards who mutter about bad rice |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technology and architecture\n\n### 3.1 Stack and folder layout\n\n- **Engine:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff package (`github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`), the full\n  readable engine `my-3d2dge.js` (one file, no dependencies). Read its `API.md` whole, `kits/stealth.js` whole (it\n  already has guards with `E.sees` / `E.Suspicion`, FlowField chasing, takedowns, parry, Shell HUD, layered music) and\n  `docs/ASSETS.md` whole. Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names. The game starts from the STEALTH kit's slice, reorganized into\n  the modules below (copy its patterns; delete the kit's starter shell, title menu and other slices).\n- **Multiplayer:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client `session.js` 1.4.0, pasted unmodified\n  (`raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`). The harness (`harness.html`, `bridge.js`,\n  `round.js`) is for tests only.\n- **Tooling:** Node 20+ (the machine has Node 24), Playwright with Chromium (the handoff's `package.json` pins it) for\n  the browser checks, and Python's `http.server` only for the hub harness.\n- **No other libraries, no external fonts, no image or audio files.** Everything is drawn and synthesized in code.\n\n```text\n<root>/                                        (the folder holding TASK.md and this PLAN.md)\n  Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734.html   final single file (built)\n  exit-interview.json\n  Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734/       dev folder\n    engine/my-3d2dge.js        copy of the handoff engine, patched (section 3.3); engine/PATCHES.md lists every change\n    vendor/aihub/session.js    unmodified client; harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (tests only)\n    handoff/                   API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, docs/ASSETS.md, kits/stealth.js, tools/*.mjs (check,\n                               filmstrip, replay, asset-sheet, asset-find), package.json: reference + tools\n    src/                       the game, in load order (section 3.4)\n    index.html                 dev page: loads engine + each src file with <script> tags (works from file://)\n    tools/build.mjs            bundles into the single HTML in <root>\n    tests/run.mjs              THE test command (section 9) + tests/*.test.mjs + tests/browser/*.mjs\n    shots/                     screenshots and filmstrips (output)\n```\n\nEnvironment rules (from TASK.md):\n\n- Read nothing outside your folder that you don't need; other agents share this machine.\n- Prefer `file://` and headless tools.\n- The hub harness needs a server. Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from the folder being served, parse\n  the port it prints, and confirm the served page is your game before trusting a result.\n- Stop only the processes you started, by PID. Never use `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n- `/tmp` on this machine is a small, nearly full tmpfs. Keep temp files inside the dev folder.\n\n### 3.2 Build and bundle (`tools/build.mjs`)\n\nOne command, `node tools/build.mjs`, writes `<root>/Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734.html`:\n\n```html\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* session.js, byte-for-byte unmodified (starts with \"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0\") */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Silent kills, unseen, fast: top ninja score wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move WASD/stick · Strike click/□ · Jump Space/✕ · Crouch C/○ · Tool R/R2\">\n<title>Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins</title>\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n</head><body>\n<!-- E.bootSplash('BENTOU 2') markup -->\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js (patched) */</script>\n<script>/* the game: src/*.js concatenated, in order, inside ONE IIFE: (() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge; ... })(); */</script>\n</body></html>\n```\n\n- Escape every `</script` inside the inlined code as `<\\/script`.\n- The session client must be the **first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`**, unmodified.\n- The goal meta is at most 60 characters and the howto meta at most 80.\n- `tools/build.mjs --js` writes only the concatenated game script to `dev/build/game.js`. The tests load that, so tests\n  and the bundle run the same code.\n- The build fails loudly if a `src` file is missing from the order list or if `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|lorem` appears in\n  `src`.\n\n### 3.3 Engine patches (do them in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, mark each `// BENTOU PATCH n`, list them in `PATCHES.md` and on the About screen)\n\n1. **Pixel font glyphs.** Add `✕ ○ □ △` to the 5×7 font `G57` (7-row bitmaps), so `input.label()` text (which returns\n   them for PlayStation pads) renders in canvas text and dialogs instead of `?`.\n2. **Button symbols setting.** In `STANDARD_SETTINGS.glyphs`, make the default `'playstation'` and the options\n   `[['playstation','PlayStation'],['xbox','Xbox']]`. TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs, with an option for Xbox A B X Y.\n3. **Humanoid gear** (in the head and weapon draw code, around the face block that draws eyes and mouth):\n   - `mask: { color, style: 'cloth' | 'oni' }`. Cloth covers nose and mouth and keeps the eyes; it skips the mouth and\n     also draws in portraits. Oni draws a red face with tusks, heavy brows and glowing eyes.\n   - New hats: `hat: 'jingasa'` (wide shallow cone) and `hat: 'kabuto'` (helmet with a crest; `crest` color).\n   - New weapons:\n     - `weapon: 'spear'` (yari: a staff with a blade tip);\n     - `weapon: 'bow'` (a curved stave with a string to the draw hand; drawn while `point` is true);\n     - `weapon: 'club'` (kanabo: thick, tapered, studded).\n   - `offhand: { len }`: a second short blade in the left hand (twin kodachi, twin kama).\n   - `sashimono: color`: a small back banner on a pole (samurai).\n\n   Check each with `node handoff/tools/filmstrip.mjs` and the Animation Lab views.\n4. **Shell: custom rows.** In `Shell._render`, add `if (s.rows) for (const k of v(s.rows)) add(this._row(k));`, so a\n   custom screen can show settings rows (sliders, toggles, choices). In `_settingsRows`, skip the group `'Dev'`, so dev\n   sliders never appear in the player's Settings.\n5. **Shell: hover moves focus.** Add a `pointermove` listener on the screen that focuses the focusable under the\n   pointer (`preventScroll: true`). TASK.md requires that hover moves the focus.\n6. **Shell: 10-foot scale.** Add a CSS variable `--ui` (default\n   `clamp(1, (innerHeight/720) * userScale, 3)`) and apply it with `zoom: var(--ui)` on `.esh-mod`, `.esh-ttl>div`,\n   `.esh-toast`, `.esh-pr`, `.esh-tut`. Recompute it on resize. `userScale` comes from the setting \"Interface size\"\n   (Normal 1, Large 1.25, Huge 1.5). Raise the base font to 16 px and buttons to a minimum height of 52 px.\n7. **Music track envelopes.** In `_note`, honor per-track `pluck: true` (non-held exponential decay over\n   `ring`, default 1.1 s), `attack` (default .006) and `release`. Koto, shamisen and harp plucks then ring and decay.\n   Shakuhachi uses a slow attack (.09) with `vib`.\n8. **Voice bus.** Expose `audio.voiceBus` (a gain on `_master`, created in `_init`), and apply the game setting\n   `voices` (0–1) to it. The voice synth (section 5.17) connects there.\n9. **Hub pause guard.** While `window.AIHub && AIHub.active` and `Pad8` (Create) is held, ignore the `pause` action\n   (Options). The hub owns Create + Options.\n\nKeep every patch small, and don't refactor the engine.\n\n### 3.4 Module map (`src/`, concatenated in this order inside one IIFE)\n\n| File | Responsibility | Key exports (on the shared `B` namespace object) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `00-core.js` | namespace `B`, registries `B.def(kind, id, spec)` / `B.get(kind, id)` / `B.all(kind)`, event bus `B.on/off/emit`, `rand()` (gameplay, Math.random) vs `crand` (cosmetic E.rng stream), math helpers | `B`, `def`, `bus` |\n| `01-tune.js` | every balance number as a `game.settings` entry in group `'Dev'` (section 5.20 table), `B.T(key)` getter with difficulty multipliers | `TUNE`, `T()` |\n| `02-input.js` | action map (section 4.1), wheel listener, `B.intentFromInput()` (stick + keys, d-pad excluded in play), device and touch-only detection, \"any input\" clock for attract | `PlayerInput` |\n| `03-glyphs.js` | pixel button icons per device and family; `B.glyph(g, action, x, y, o)`, and inline `{a:jump}` tokens in canvas text | `Glyph` |\n| `04-camera.js` | follow, 45-degree rotation, zoom, look-ahead (mouse lean, Focus + right stick), cinematic overrides (Silent Cut zoom, boss intro, cutscenes) | `Cam` |\n| `10-audio.js` | `audio.define` sfx set, songs with layers (section 5.17), `B.music.mood(level)` | `Sfx`, `Songs`, `Music` |\n| `11-voice.js` | gibberish formant voice synth, speaker profiles, dialog hook, barks with distance and panning | `Voice` |\n| `20-assets.js` | `E.SHAPES` / `E.MATERIALS` / `E.PATTERNS` for Japanese props, floor textures, wall `decorate` functions, the kawara roof-cap renderer, string sprites (item icons, crest, kanji, moon, eyes) | `Art` |\n| `21-rigs.js` | character factories (section 6.1), `Hound` quadruped class, joint post-processing helpers (arms-back ninja run, wall-hug pose, eating, sleeping, mouth cover) | `Rigs`, `Hound` |\n| `30-world.js` | level JSON → `World` (TileMap + navigation map + light map + hide map + water + anchors + props + lights + zones); queries (`lightAt`, `isHide`, `isDeep`, `anchorsNear`, `nearestBell`, `zoneAt`) | `World` |\n| `31-actors.js` | base `Actor` (a Mover plus rig plus HP plus status); spawn helpers | `Actor` |\n| `40-hero.js` | hero controller from an *intent* (section 5.1): traversal, swim, hug, drag, focus, noise emission, tool use, combat hooks | `Hero` |\n| `41-silentcut.js` | Silent Cut detection and `E.ACTIONS` entries per variant and character; cinematic and splash | `SilentCut` |\n| `42-grapple.js` | anchor search, targeting UI, `E.ACTIONS.grapple`, rope drawing | `Grapple` |\n| `43-combat.js` | damage pipeline (`B.damage(src, dst, amount, kind)`), hero combos and jump attack, block, parry, riposte, dodge, i-frames, hit fx | `Combat` |\n| `44-tools.js` | the 10 tools: data and behavior (projectiles, lobs, clouds, traps, baits), `Bento` loadout model | `Tools`, `Bento` |\n| `50-perception.js` | sight (exposure from light, crouch, cover, motion, look-up limit, smoke), hearing (`B.noise(x,y,z,loud,kind)`), smell, body discovery, Shadow Sight visibility, Ki values | `Perception` |\n| `51-guard-brain.js` | guard state machine on top of `E.Suspicion` (section 5.4), patrol, post, sleep, eat, chat, search, chase, fight, flee, bark scheduling, alarm and bell logic | `Brain` |\n| `52-enemies.js` | archetype registry: ashigaru, samurai, archer, ninja, hound, civilians, disguised | `def('enemy',...)` |\n| `53-bosses.js` | `Boss` base with phases and pattern scripts (`game.script` generators); Ittetsu, Gonroku, Hotaru, Kurogane | `def('boss',...)` |\n| `54-escort.js` | the escort follower (Tobei) | `Escort` |\n| `60-mission.js` | mission runtime: objectives, triggers, timers, checkpoints, fail states, pickups, interactions | `Mission` |\n| `61-score.js` | scoring events → score, ranks, unlocks, best records, results data | `Score` |\n| `62-story.js` | all text: crawl, briefings, cutscene scripts, boss lines, barks, results comments (section 6.6) | `Story` |\n| `63-cutscene.js` | cutscene player (staged rigs, camera tweens, letterbox, `E.Dialog` with portraits and voices, skip) | `Cutscene` |\n| `64-levels-*.js` | one file per level: training, m1, m2, m3, delivery (data only, `def('level', id, {...})`) | level data |\n| `65-missions.js` | mission metadata (`def('mission', id, {...})`): title, level, briefing, loadout hint, par, unlock rules, next | mission data |\n| `70-hud.js` | canvas HUD (section 4.4): health, Ki gauge, tool box, prompts, tutorial cards, toasts, boss bar, timer, breath, stamina, awareness marks, threat arrows, letterbox, splash | `Hud` |\n| `71-scenes-menu.js` | boot, title (idle timer), main menu, character select, mission select, about/credits, touch-only notice | scenes |\n| `72-scenes-story.js` | briefing, bento packing, results, game over, ending and credits | scenes |\n| `73-scene-mission.js` | the gameplay scene used by story, trial, hub, attract and workshop test play | `MissionScene` |\n| `74-dev.js` | dev mode screens, cheats, overlays, sliders (section 5.20) | `Dev` |\n| `75-workshop.js` | the Mission Editor (section 5.21) | scene `workshop` |\n| `80-autopilot.js` | intent-producing autopilot (beats), shared by attract mode and the playthrough test; per-mission routes | `Autopilot` |\n| `81-attract.js` | attract director and vignettes (section 5.19) | scene `attract` |\n| `82-hub.js` | AI Hub ghost mode, own card, ghost send and draw, progress and result, end handling; Shadow Trial ghost recording | `Hub`, scene `hubCard` |\n| `90-main.js` | `new E.Game(...)`, scene registration, boot steps, saves wiring, `game.debug`, `window.__BENTOU` | — |\n\nArchitecture rules (the Emberdeep lessons from AI_GUIDE):\n\n- **A spine, then content.** Content (levels, enemies, tools, bosses, lines) is data in registries and never edits the\n  core. Systems talk through the **event bus**:\n\n  ```text\n  noise, seen, detected, alert, bodyFound, silentCut, kill, damage, heroDeath, toolUsed,\n  objective, checkpoint, bell, boss, missionEnd\n  ```\n\n  Score, HUD toasts, music mood, barks, hub progress and tests all listen. None of them is called directly from the\n  combat or AI code.\n- **One intent interface for the hero.** The player's input adapter, the autopilot and the tests all produce the same\n  intent object (section 5.1), so attract mode never touches `game.input` and can't be mistaken for player input.\n- **Game logic in world units, with `dt` everywhere.** Gameplay randomness uses `rand()` in update only; cosmetic\n  randomness in draw uses `crand` (an `E.rng` stream). Draw code never consumes `Math.random`, which keeps hub-seeded\n  runs and tests deterministic at any refresh rate.\n- **No DOM at load in headless.** Guard every `matchMedia`, `document` and `navigator` use, so the game runs under\n  `node:vm` (as `game/test.mjs` does).\n\n### 3.5 Scenes and flow\n\n```text\nboot ─┬─(AIHub.active)──► hubCard ──start──► mission(mode:'hub') ──end──► hub results overlay\n      └─► title ◄──────── any input ──── attract (after 10 s idle on title or main menu)\n           │ menu: Continue · New Story · Missions · Shadow Trial · Workshop · Settings · About\n           ├─ New Story ─► charSelect ─► story(crawl+prologue) ─► briefing ─► bento ─► mission ─► results ─► story ─► …\n           │                                                     (training → m1 → m2 → m3 → ending+credits → title)\n           ├─ Missions ─► missionSelect (character + mission, best ranks) ─► briefing ─► bento ─► mission ─► results\n           ├─ Shadow Trial ─► bento(trial rules) ─► mission(mode:'trial', with your best ghost) ─► results(trial board)\n           ├─ Workshop ─► workshop ◄─► mission(mode:'workshop')\n           └─ About ─► about (pages)\nmission: pausable. Pause = Shell pause: Resume · Restart from checkpoint · Restart mission · Objectives · Dev Mode ·\n         Settings · Controls · Full screen · Quit to title   (hub: Resume · Settings · Controls only)\nmission death ─► \"Your box is empty\" overlay: Retry from checkpoint · Restart mission · Quit\n```\n\nScene options:\n\n- `mission`:\n\n  ```js\n  { pausable: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'], res: 'ps1', expand: true, input: B.INPUT,\n    touch: [], camera: { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1.15, tall: 1.35, rotate: true, wheel: false } }\n  ```\n\n- Menu scenes use the same input preset and `touch: []`.\n- The title is a side-view diorama (`view: 'side'`) with a `PlatformMap` ledge and an `E.Backdrop`.\n\n### 3.6 Data formats (the campaign and the Workshop share them exactly)\n\n**Level** (`def('level', id, spec)`; the Workshop exports the same JSON):\n\n```js\n{ id: 'm1', name: 'Rice and Ash', size: [56, 48], time: 'night' /* dusk | night | rain | festival */, ambient: .38,\n  rows: ['########…', …],                 // terrain only, default legend below (48 strings of 56 chars)\n  zones: [{ id: 'mansion', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], name: 'Kanemori Mansion' }],   // HUD place names\n  lights: [{ at: [cx, cy], z: 18, r: 64, i: .9, color: '#ffb060', kind: 'stoneLantern' }],   // kind also places its prop\n  props: [['stoneLantern', cx, cy, { facing: 0 }], ['bamboo', cx, cy], …],   // solid unless { solid: false }\n  anchors: [[cx, cy, z]],                // extra grapple anchors (tree crowns, beams); roof edges are found automatically\n  hero: { at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 0 }, exit: { at: [cx, cy], r: 1.5 },\n  guards: [{ id: 'g1', type: 'ashigaru', at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 90, mode: 'patrol', lantern: true,\n             route: [[cx, cy, wait, lookDeg], …], loop: true, partner: null, faction: 'kanemori' }],\n  civilians: [{ id: 'c1', type: 'maid', at: [cx, cy], mode: 'idle', route: null, disguised: false }],\n  pickups: [{ id: 'ledger', kind: 'story', at: [cx, cy], z: 0 }, { kind: 'tool', tool: 'riceball', n: 2, at: [cx, cy] }],\n  bells: [[cx, cy]], barracks: [[cx, cy]],          // alarm bell spots; where reinforcements come out\n  interact: [{ id: 'lever', at: [cx, cy], hold: 1.2, text: 'Open the water gate', do: [['open', cx, cy, w, h]] }],\n  escort: { id: 'tobei', at: [cx, cy], hp: 60 },\n  boss: { id: 'gonroku', at: [cx, cy], arena: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], start: 'trigger:court' },\n  objectives: [{ id: 'kill', type: 'assassinate', target: 'kanemori', text: 'Silence Magistrate Kanemori' },\n               { id: 'letter', type: 'retrieve', pickup: 'ledger', optional: true, text: 'Find what he hides' },\n               { id: 'escape', type: 'reach', exit: true, after: ['kill', 'boss'], text: 'Escape by the canal boat' }],\n  triggers: [{ id: 'court', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], once: true,\n               do: [['checkpoint'], ['boss', 'gonroku'], ['say', 'gonroku', 'gon_intro']] }],\n  timer: null,            // { seconds: 720, fail: 'text', stopOn: 'objective:sake' }\n  par: 600, music: 'm1', weather: null }\n```\n\nTrigger conditions:\n\n- `rect` / `at+r` (enter);\n- `when: 'objective:<id>'`;\n- `'kill:<id>'`;\n- `'alert'`;\n- `'time:<s>'`;\n- `'pickup:<id>'`.\n\nTrigger actions:\n\n- `say`, `toast`, `tutorial`;\n- `checkpoint`;\n- `spawn` (a guard spec);\n- `boss`, `cutscene`;\n- `objective` (`show` | `done` | `fail`);\n- `open` / `close` (`map.set` cells);\n- `music` (layer);\n- `flag`.\n\n**Default legend** (rows are terrain; actors are listed in the entity arrays):\n\n| Char | What | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.` | earth path | normal footsteps |\n| `,` | tall grass | hide: crouched exposure ×0.15, standing ×0.6 |\n| `\"` | bamboo grove | hide like grass; bamboo props scattered automatically (seeded by cell) |\n| `:` | raked gravel | noise ×1.6; even crouch-walking makes noise 12 |\n| `=` | wooden boards (engawa, pier) | noise ×1.2 when running; creak sfx |\n| `_` | tatami (inside halls) | noise ×0.6 |\n| `+` | stone paving | normal |\n| `~` | deep water | swim/dive; guards and hounds never enter (nav map blocks it) |\n| `-` | shallow water | wade: speed ×0.7, splash noise 40 even walking, no hiding |\n| `#` | castle / outer stone wall (ishigaki) | h 56, face granite stone, top slab, `cut: true, cutH: 8`; grapple only |\n| `W` | compound wall, plaster with tile cap | h 30 (climbable ledge), face plaster, roof tiles, `cut: true, cutH: 6` |\n| `F` | bamboo fence | h 14 (vaulted at a run) |\n| `H` | hall wall (enterable building perimeter) | h 40, face timber with shoji `decorate`, `cut: true, cutH: 6`; its roof cap is visual (section 5.18) |\n| `d` | doorway in a hall wall | floor `door`; drawn as an open sliding door |\n| `A` | townhouse (machiya) | h 40, plaster and timber with lattice, kawara roof (walkable) |\n| `B` | two-story house or inn | h 64, timber and plaster, balcony, kawara roof |\n| `C` | storehouse (kura) | h 48, white plaster with a namako band, heavy kawara roof |\n| `D` | shop with noren curtain | h 40, timber, noren `decorate`, kawara roof |\n| `S` | shrine or temple hall | h 56, vermilion pillars, dark kawara roof |\n| `T` | watchtower (yagura), 2×2 | h 80, plank, small roof; archers stand on top |\n| `G` / `K` / `M` | castle keep tiers | h 64 / 112 / 160; ishigaki base to z 24, then white plaster; chidori gables; golden shachihoko on `M` |\n| `P` | planter or stone platform | h 10 (jump up; cover when crouched behind it) |\n| `R` | rocks | h 20, face rock, climbable |\n\nEvery solid building has a flat walkable top at its height. \"No passages under things\" is an engine rule, so halls are\nenterable but their roofs are not walkable.\n\n**Guard / enemy archetype** (`def('enemy', id, spec)`):\n\n```js\n{ rig, hp, walk, run, sight: { range, fov, lookUp }, hear, smell, moves: [...], ranged, climbs, faction, barks,\n  canSilentCut: true }\n```\n\n**Tool** (`def('tool', id, spec)`):\n\n```js\n{ name, icon, stack, use: 'eat' | 'throw' | 'lob' | 'drop' | 'self', range, effect(ctx), unlock }\n```\n\n**Mission** (`def('mission', id, spec)`):\n\n```js\n{ title, level, briefing, debrief, loadoutHint: [...], par, next, unlocks: [{ tool, rank }] }\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Controls and UX: controller first, 10 feet from a TV\n\n### 4.1 Action map (`B.INPUT`, passed as `new E.Game({ input })`; every action is rebindable on the standard Controls screen)\n\n| Action | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (Settings) | Keyboard + mouse | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Move | Left stick (tilt <55% = quiet walk) | Left stick | WASD / arrows | in play the d-pad does **not** move: the hero reads the stick and keys only |\n| Camera | Right stick: ←/→ flick turns 45°, ↑/↓ zooms | Right stick | Q / E turn 45°, − / = zoom; mouse leans the view toward the cursor | R3 / X resets the camera |\n| Jump · climb · vault | ✕ (Pad0) | A | Space | parkour first (ledge ≤ 30, vault ≤ 14, gap leap) |\n| Crouch (toggle; hold in Settings) | ○ (Pad1) | B | C | **never bind Ctrl**: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab |\n| Strike · Silent Cut · riposte | □ (Pad2) | X | Left click / J | context: the prompt says which |\n| Interact (drag body, pick up, open, talk, lever) | △ (Pad3) | Y | F (or left click on a highlighted thing) | |\n| Block (hold) · parry (timed) | L1 (Pad4) | LB | Right click / K | block + jump + direction = dodge roll |\n| Grappling hook (tap: fire at the highlighted anchor; hold: aim) | R1 (Pad5) | RB | G / middle click | with the mouse: the anchor under the cursor |\n| Ki Focus (hold) | L2 (Pad6) | LT | Tab | slows to a walk; sense radius 220; right stick or mouse scouts further |\n| Use tool | R2 (Pad7) | RT | R | thrown at the cursor (mouse) or auto-aimed (pad/keys) |\n| Sprint | L3 (Pad10, a toggle until the stick is released) | LS | Shift (hold) | stamina |\n| Previous / next tool | D-pad ← / → | D-pad | mouse wheel, 1–8 picks a compartment | |\n| Eat a rice ball (quick heal) | D-pad ↓ | D-pad ↓ | H | |\n| Whistle (lure) | D-pad ↑ | D-pad ↑ | V | noise 70 at the hero: lures nearby guards to search |\n| Objectives | Create (Pad8) | View | M | shows the objectives panel (in a hub session Create does nothing: the hub owns Create + Options) |\n| Pause | Options (Pad9) | Menu | Esc / P | engine standard (hub: ignored while Create is held) |\n| Menus | d-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | A / B | arrows, Enter, Esc; mouse hover focuses, click picks | |\n\nImplementation notes:\n\n- Action names, in `B.INPUT` and on the Controls screen (`menu.controls` gives the names):\n\n  | Action | Controls name |\n  |---|---|\n  | `jump` | Jump / climb |\n  | `crouch` | Crouch |\n  | `attack` | Strike / Silent Cut |\n  | `interact` | Interact |\n  | `block` | Block / parry |\n  | `grapple` | Grappling hook |\n  | `focus` | Ki Focus |\n  | `useTool` | Use tool |\n  | `sprint` | Sprint |\n  | `toolPrev` | Previous tool |\n  | `toolNext` | Next tool |\n  | `heal` | Eat rice ball |\n  | `lure` | Whistle |\n  | `camLeft` | Turn camera left |\n  | `camRight` | Turn camera right |\n  | `camReset` | Reset camera |\n  | `objectives` | Objectives |\n\n  The engine adds `up/down/left/right/start/pause/confirm/cancel`. Its menu actions `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z,\n  pad A) and `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B) overlap some play keys; that is harmless, because play never\n  reads them.\n- Movement in play is `B.intentFromInput()`: the left stick from `input.padAxes` with the radial deadzone, plus the\n  key codes of the `up/down/left/right` actions that are not `Pad*`, through `game.view.screenDirToGround`. Menus still\n  use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the d-pad.\n- Tool cycling with the wheel: set `camera.wheel: false` on the mission scene and add a passive `wheel` listener that\n  taps `toolPrev` / `toolNext`.\n- `input.lastDevice` decides prompts. A mouse used in the last 3 s means \"mouse mode\": cursor aiming, hover highlights\n  and camera lean. A stick or key press ends it.\n- Mouse in the world:\n  - Hovering a guard shows its awareness meter and type label.\n  - Hovering a highlighted interactable within reach changes the left click from Strike to Interact.\n  - Hovering a valid roof edge or anchor highlights it for G / middle click.\n  - Strikes face the cursor (Diablo-style).\n  - Thrown tools land at `game.mouseGround()`, clamped to range.\n\n### 4.2 Glyphs and prompts (`03-glyphs.js`)\n\n- Every prompt, tutorial card, menu footer and dialog token follows the last device used, and redraws the moment it\n  changes.\n- **Pad (PlayStation):** a dark circle with a colored symbol: ✕ blue `#7ab4ff`, ○ red `#ff6a6a`, □ pink `#ff8ad8`,\n  △ green `#5ae0a0`.\n- **Pad (Xbox):** A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow.\n- **Shoulders, triggers and buttons:** L1/R1/L2/R2 (LB/RB/LT/RT) are rounded tabs. Sticks are rings with an arrow.\n  The d-pad is a cross with the used arm lit. Create/Options (View/Menu) are pills.\n- **Keyboard:** a light keycap with `input.codeLabel(code)`.\n- **Mouse:** a mouse icon with the left, right or middle button lit, or the wheel.\n- Icons are 9–11 game pixels tall and drawn with `E.px` (no font dependency). Canvas text can embed `{a:attack}`,\n  which renders that action's icon inline.\n- HTML (Shell) text uses `input.label()` (Unicode is fine there).\n\n### 4.3 Screens (big, sparse, one decision per screen; never dense web-style tables)\n\nCanvas screens use `E.Menu`, which already moves its cursor on hover and picks on click. HTML screens (pause, settings,\ncontrols, dev, objectives, Workshop menus, About) use one `E.Shell` with this theme:\n\n```js\n{ ink: '#f4ead5', paper: 'rgba(20,12,12,.92)', accent: '#e8b04a', muted: '#b8a890', danger: '#d8402a',\n  line: 'rgba(232,176,74,.35)', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: 'Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' }\n```\n\n- **Title** (canvas, side view):\n  - A night sky with a big moon over a castle silhouette (custom `E.Backdrop`: moon, stars, mountains, castle, fog).\n  - Sojiro and Kaede on a tiled ridge in front, scarves fluttering, cherry petals falling.\n  - The logo is `E.font.title('BENTOU 2', … { scale: 4, colors: gold → vermilion, depth: 3 })` with the subtitle below\n    and the clan crest stamp.\n  - \"PRESS {a:start}\" first, then the `E.Menu`: Continue · New Story · Missions · Shadow Trial · Workshop · Settings\n    (`game.menu('settings')`) · About. Missing items are hidden (no Continue without a save).\n  - Version line: `E.versionLabel()` + game version, small, bottom right.\n- **Character select:**\n  - Two rigs on a rooftop, side by side; ←/→ or hover picks one.\n  - Name, weapon, three short bars (Strength, Speed, Stealth) and one sentence.\n  - A spoken gibberish greeting with a subtitle.\n- **Mission select:** a vertical list of unlocked missions on a scroll. Each shows its best rank stamp per character\n  and the character toggle (L1/R1).\n- **Briefing:**\n  - A painted interior (the shop's back room: shoji, stacked boxes, a lantern; or the lord's moonlit garden) with live\n    portraits (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n  - `E.Dialog` lines with names and voices, then an objectives card (2–3 lines).\n  - Hold {a:start} to skip.\n- **Pack the Bento:**\n  - A black-lacquer two-tier box seen from above; each tier has 4 compartments.\n  - The left column is the tool shelf (big icons, name, one-line effect). The stick moves, ✕ fills the focused\n    compartment, ○ empties it, △ restores the mission's suggested loadout, Options starts.\n  - Mouse: hover focuses, click places, right click empties.\n  - Shows each stack count. The last loadout is remembered.\n- **Results:**\n  - A scroll unrolls. One stat line appears at a time with a brush underline: Time, Silent Cuts, Kills, Times detected,\n    Civilians harmed, Optional tasks, Tools used, Retries. Then the score counts up.\n  - The rank hanko slams down (screen thump, stamp sound).\n  - Granny's one-line comment, and a \"New tool\" card if one unlocked.\n  - Buttons: Continue · Retry · Missions.\n- **Game over overlay:** time slows, the screen desaturates, \"YOUR BOX IS EMPTY\" in brush type, and three choices.\n- **About / Credits:** paged (◀ ▶), one section per page, large type (section 5.23).\n- **Ending:** cutscene, then a credits roll over the moon. Any input speeds it up; it returns to the title.\n\n### 4.4 In-game HUD (canvas, anchored to `r.W` / `r.H`, inside 4% overscan margins)\n\n| Where | Element |\n|---|---|\n| top left | health bar (brush stroke in vermilion, the character's crest at its head); below it **静斬 ×n** (Silent Cut count) |\n| top center | objective toast on change (fades after 4 s); the boss bar (wide, the name in brush caps, phase ticks); \"ALARM!\" banner |\n| top right | M3 moon timer (an arc with the moon's position; turns red under 60 s); place name on entering a zone (fades) |\n| bottom left | **Ki Gauge**: an 18-px-radius semicircle with the number 0–99 in large digits (font scale 2), a colored ring and `?`/`!`; the eye icon in its middle shows your light (closed = shadow, half = dim, open = lit) |\n| bottom right | **tool box**: the selected tool's icon (16 px at scale 2) with its count; neighbors slide by on change; d-pad glyphs |\n| bottom center | context prompts (at most 2): icon + label (\"□ Silent Cut — Back\", \"R1 Grapple\", \"△ Drag body\", \"△ Hold: open gate\" with a progress ring) |\n| over the hero | breath bubbles when diving; a stamina ring when <100 |\n| over guards | `?` yellow (notice), `?` orange (search), `!` red (alert), `Zz` (asleep), `…` (eating), with a small suspicion bar; tinted by Shadow Sight state |\n| screen edges | red chevrons toward alerted enemies off screen; `r.marker` objective diamond (Settings: Objective marker) |\n| cinematic | letterbox bars (Silent Cuts, boss intros, cutscenes); the 静斬 splash; a red edge pulse when hit |\n\nThe objectives panel (Create/M) is an `E.Shell` screen: the mission title, objectives with checkmarks, the time, and\nSilent Cuts so far. In the pause menu it is \"Objectives\".\n\n### 4.5 Touch-only devices\n\n- Detection: `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, with no gamepad connected\n  and no key pressed yet.\n- Then: `input.touchEnabled = false`, and no scene declares touch buttons.\n- The title replaces its menu with a large panel: **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, a line (\"Connect a controller\n  or a keyboard to play.\"), and a big **Settings** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). The engine corner menu button\n  stays.\n- Attract mode runs after 10 s as usual, and a tap returns to the title.\n- `gamepadconnected` or any key press removes the notice at once.\n\n### 4.6 Settings (the engine's standard screens plus ours in group \"Game\"; Sound gets \"Voices\")\n\n| Setting | Values (default first) |\n|---|---|\n| Button symbols *(engine, patched)* | PlayStation · Xbox |\n| Interface size | Auto · Normal · Large · Huge |\n| Difficulty | Ninja · Novice · Grand Master: guard perception ×1 / .8 / 1.2, damage taken ×1 / .6 / 1.4, Ki range ×1 / 1.2 / .85 |\n| Camera angle | Low (iso) · High (threequarter) |\n| Invert camera turn | Off · On |\n| Crouch | Toggle · Hold |\n| Sight cones | On · Off (the faint cones of guards you can see) |\n| Objective marker | On · Off |\n| Show all enemies (assist) | Off · On (Shadow Sight off) |\n| Ki heartbeat | On · Off |\n| Text speed | Normal · Slow · Fast |\n| Blood | Ink · Off (red ink splashes and decals) |\n| Voices *(Sound)* | slider 0–1, default .8 |\n\n### 4.7 Camera\n\n- `game.follow(hero, { z: 18, lead: 10 })`, `cam.smooth = .12`, `cam.bounds = v => world.map.bounds(v)`.\n- **Turn:** `game.rotateView(±45)` with a .25 s cooldown and a short whoosh. The compass on the tool box shows north.\n  Movement stays screen-relative through `screenDirToGround`.\n- **Zoom:** .75–2×, starting at 1.15 (1.35 on a tall screen). Right stick ↑/↓ or −/=.\n- **Look-ahead:** mouse mode leans the focus toward the cursor by up to 40 units (140 with Focus). Pad: Focus + right\n  stick pans up to 140 units, eased back on release.\n- **Cinematics:**\n  - Silent Cut: zoom tween to 1.8× in .15 s, `timeScale = T('slowmo')` for .55 s, letterbox, then restore.\n  - Boss intro: a `game.tween` pan to the boss, the name card, then a pan back.\n  - Cutscenes: scripted focus and zoom.\n  - Respect Reduce motion: no shake, shorter zooms.\n- **Occlusion:**\n  - The hero always draws with `xray: { actors: true }`. Visible guards draw with `xray: { color: <awareness color> }`.\n  - Walls nearest the camera use `cut`.\n  - Hall roof caps fade while the hero is inside that hall (section 5.18).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Systems\n\nNumbers marked *T* are live dev sliders (section 5.20). Every system emits bus events and is covered by tests (section 9).\n\n### 5.1 Hero, intent and traversal (`40-hero.js`)\n\n**Intent** (built by `PlayerInput`, `Autopilot` or a test):\n","numLines":600,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1886}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GtiPdkjubvn64YPq4TR1Vp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
