n":"Grep key API signatures from index"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019HtPqU72BJDwgmFccw5nQg","type":"tool_result","content":"278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n330:- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n335:- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n564:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n566:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' }\n773:- `map.wall(from, dir, o = {})` †: the wall face a body touches or faces: from `from`, in direction dir (an angle or [dx, dy]), the first point within reach whose top rises more than a step above its feet. { x, y (on the face), nx, ny (the face's normal, out toward the body), top (how high it rises there), bottom (the floor at its foot), facing (the angle into it) } or null. Cells give axis faces; a map.solid box\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leaps; a press in the ai\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n964:- `mover.dodge(dir, dist = 34)` †: a dodge roll toward dir (an angle or [dx, dy]; default its facing) when it stands free. Returns the action, or null\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n966:- `mover.respawn()` †: back to the last safe spot (after water, a pit, a fall it shouldn't survive)\n967:- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n969:- `mover.accel = 700`, `mover.airAccel = 260` †: how fast it gets there\n970:- `mover.action = null` †: the E.Action playing, or null\n971:- `mover.buffer = .12` †: seconds a jump press is kept\n972:- `mover.climb = true` †: climbs ledges (true)\n973:- `mover.climbAny = false` †: climbs any wall face (see the section's header)\n974:- `mover.climbMax = 82` †: the highest ledge it climbs\n975:- `mover.climbSpeed = 34` †: its climbing speed\n976:- `mover.coyote = .1` †: seconds a jump still works after leaving an edge\n977:- `mover.crouch = false` †: sneaking (a toggle)\n978:- `mover.exhausted = false` †: out of stamina until a third is back\n979:- `mover.facing = 0` †: the angle it faces\n980:- `mover.fell = 0`, `mover.hurt = false`, `mover.inHazard = false` †: what happened this step\n981:- `mover.gapAssist = true` †: a jump at a gap aims for the far side\n982:- `mover.glide = false` †: opens a glide in the air (see the header)\n983:- `mover.glideMin = 24`, `mover.glideSink = 26`, `mover.glideSpeed = 72` †: how high over the ground it opens, how fast it sinks and flies\n984:- `mover.gliding = false` †: gliding now\n985:- `mover.hopMax = 48` †: drops up to this deep are hopped down\n986:- `mover.hurtAt = 72`, `mover.rollAt = 26` †: fall heights that roll and that hurt\n987:- `mover.jumpSpeed = 220` †: a jump's upward speed\n988:- `mover.lastSafe = null` †: the last spot it stood safely, for respawn()\n989:- `mover.lift = 0` †: an updraft's rising speed (a number, or a function of the mover)\n990:- `mover.run = 85`, `mover.sneak = 32`, `mover.sprintSpeed = 125`, `mover.walk = 50` †: top speeds (world units a second)\n991:- `mover.sprinting = false` †: sprinting now\n992:- `mover.stamina` †: what is left (full to start)\n993:- `mover.staminaMax = 0` †: its stamina (0: none)\n994:- `mover.staminaRegen = 35` †: refilled a second standing\n995:- `mover.tire` †: { climb, climbJump, glide, sprint } it costs\n996:- `mover.turn = 14` †: how fast it turns, radians a second\n997:- `mover.vault = 14` †: walls up to this high are vaulted at a run\n998:- `mover.wall = null` †: the face it holds on to (map.wall's), or null\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget se\n1014:- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1108:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1110:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'm\n1112:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1113:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n1114:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1115:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1118:- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n1119:- `talk.game`: its game\n1120:- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n1121:- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n1122:- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n1123:- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n1124:- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n1125:- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n1126:- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n1127:- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n1128:- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n1129:- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n1130:- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n1131:- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n1132:- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n1133:- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"860bdf43-f338-4749-8dc6-eae8e6044b66","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:20.881Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n330:- `input.map`: each action's codes ({ jump: ['Space', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump'] }); every action also answers to 'Act:<name>' (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold)\n335:- `input.padAxes = []` †: the gamepad's raw axes\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under walls and bodies)\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n564:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Returns its value\n566:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' }\n773:- `map.wall(from, dir, o = {})` †: the wall face a body touches or faces: from `from`, in direction dir (an angle or [dx, dy]), the first point within reach whose top rises more than a step above its feet. { x, y (on the face), nx, ny (the face's normal, out toward the body), top (how high it rises there), bottom (the floor at its foot), facing (the angle into it) } or null. Cells give axis faces; a map.solid box\n821:- `flow.next(x, y)` †: the next cell to head for from (x, y): { x, y, z (its center and top), kind: 'walk' | 'climb' | 'drop' | 'jump', edge (how far (x, y) is from the side of its cell it leaves by) }, or null where the field doesn't reach (or at the target). An AI standing on the ground presses jump for a 'climb' or a 'jump' once edge is under its radius plus a little (E.Mover climbs or leaps; a press in the ai\n963:- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n964:- `mover.dodge(dir, dist = 34)` †: a dodge roll toward dir (an angle or [dx, dy]; default its facing) when it stands free. Returns the action, or null\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n966:- `mover.respawn()` †: back to the last safe spot (after water, a pit, a fall it shouldn't survive)\n967:- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n969:- `mover.accel = 700`, `mover.airAccel = 260` †: how fast it gets there\n970:- `mover.action = null` †: the E.Action playing, or null\n971:- `mover.buffer = .12` †: seconds a jump press is kept\n972:- `mover.climb = true` †: climbs ledges (true)\n973:- `mover.climbAny = false` †: climbs any wall face (see the section's header)\n974:- `mover.climbMax = 82` †: the highest ledge it climbs\n975:- `mover.climbSpeed = 34` †: its climbing speed\n976:- `mover.coyote = .1` †: seconds a jump still works after leaving an edge\n977:- `mover.crouch = false` †: sneaking (a toggle)\n978:- `mover.exhausted = false` †: out of stamina until a third is back\n979:- `mover.facing = 0` †: the angle it faces\n980:- `mover.fell = 0`, `mover.hurt = false`, `mover.inHazard = false` †: what happened this step\n981:- `mover.gapAssist = true` †: a jump at a gap aims for the far side\n982:- `mover.glide = false` †: opens a glide in the air (see the header)\n983:- `mover.glideMin = 24`, `mover.glideSink = 26`, `mover.glideSpeed = 72` †: how high over the ground it opens, how fast it sinks and flies\n984:- `mover.gliding = false` †: gliding now\n985:- `mover.hopMax = 48` †: drops up to this deep are hopped down\n986:- `mover.hurtAt = 72`, `mover.rollAt = 26` †: fall heights that roll and that hurt\n987:- `mover.jumpSpeed = 220` †: a jump's upward speed\n988:- `mover.lastSafe = null` †: the last spot it stood safely, for respawn()\n989:- `mover.lift = 0` †: an updraft's rising speed (a number, or a function of the mover)\n990:- `mover.run = 85`, `mover.sneak = 32`, `mover.sprintSpeed = 125`, `mover.walk = 50` †: top speeds (world units a second)\n991:- `mover.sprinting = false` †: sprinting now\n992:- `mover.stamina` †: what is left (full to start)\n993:- `mover.staminaMax = 0` †: its stamina (0: none)\n994:- `mover.staminaRegen = 35` †: refilled a second standing\n995:- `mover.tire` †: { climb, climbJump, glide, sprint } it costs\n996:- `mover.turn = 14` †: how fast it turns, radians a second\n997:- `mover.vault = 14` †: walls up to this high are vaulted at a run\n998:- `mover.wall = null` †: the face it holds on to (map.wall's), or null\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget se\n1014:- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1107:- `talk.choiceAt(i)` †: where choice i is on the screen while the choices show: [x, y] (its middle, for a test's tap), else null\n1108:- `talk.close()`: close it now (and forget pending presses, so the same press doesn't also attack)\n1109:- `talk.draw(r)`: draw it (anywhere in draw: it goes to the overlay)\n1110:- `talk.pageLen`: the letters on the page shown\n1111:- `talk.say(text, o = {})`: open with one string or a list of strings (each starts a new page). opts: { name, onDone, choices, onChoice, portrait: rig (a live close-up of that Humanoid beside the text) or a function (g, x, y, size), portraitSize: 40, portraitOpts: { zoom, turn, bg }, auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself, modal: false (play goes on while it shows: radio chatter), place: 'top' | 'm\n1112:- `talk.typing`: true while the page is still typing\n1113:- `talk.update(dt)`: type and turn pages (confirm finishes the line, then turns the page); returns true while open and modal, so gameplay can wait: if (talk.update(dt)) return;\n1114:- `talk.auto`: seconds each page stays after typing\n1115:- `talk.bg = '#141a3a'`, `talk.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the box's colors\n1116:- `talk.choice = 0`: the choice under the cursor\n1117:- `talk.choices`: the answers offered on the last page, or null\n1118:- `talk.color = '#ffffff'`: the text's color\n1119:- `talk.game`: its game\n1120:- `talk.i = 0`: the page shown\n1121:- `talk.lines = 3`: text lines per page\n1122:- `talk.modal`: false lets play go on (radio chatter)\n1123:- `talk.name`: the speaker's name shown on the box\n1124:- `talk.nameColor = '#ffd36a'`: the speaker's name's color\n1125:- `talk.onChoice`: called with the index picked\n1126:- `talk.onDone`: called when the last page closes\n1127:- `talk.open = false`: true while it shows\n1128:- `talk.pages = []`: the text wrapped into pages of lines\n1129:- `talk.place = 'bottom'`: 'bottom' | 'top' | 'middle'\n1130:- `talk.portrait`: the portrait beside the text (a Humanoid, or a function (g, x, y, size)), or null; pSize: its size in pixels; pOpts: its options ({ zoom, turn, bg })\n1131:- `talk.shown = 0`: letters typed so far on it\n1132:- `talk.speed = 50`: letters typed per second\n1133:- `talk.vars = null`: the values {$name} in the text reads (say's vars first)\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183638__x1295cd/work/KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183638/vendor/aihub/bridge.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":339,"lines":["+/**","+ * bridge.js — the hub's end of one game frame in a session.","+ *","+ * A game speaks the AI Hub Session Protocol over postMessage (lib/hub/README.md).","+ * The bridge checks every message, enforces the limits, and routes it: control","+ * messages (hello, ready, result, finish, error) to whoever coordinates the","+ * round (lib/hub/round.js), game traffic straight to the other players, and a","+ * game's answers on its own card to the page that holds it. What","+ * comes back from the network is checked again before it reaches the game,","+ * and anything from another round is dropped, so a slow packet can never land","+ * in the next game.","+ *","+ * The network is anything with `send(toKey, envelope, {reliable})`: the","+ * simulated one below (harness, tests), a BroadcastChannel between tabs, or a","+ * WebRTC mesh. Envelopes:","+ *   {k:'c', r, m}       to the coordinator: a message from this game","+ *   {k:'h', r, m}       from the coordinator: welcome, start, leave, time-up, end","+ *   {k:'g', r, f, d}    game traffic from player id f","+ *   {k:'p', r, f, d}    player id f's progress, {score, label}, for the scoreboard","+ */","+","+export const LIMITS = Object.freeze({","+  maxBytes: 16_384,","+  ratePerS: 20,","+  burst: 40,","+  queueMessages: 64,","+  queueBytes: 262_144,","+  /**","+   * progress() reaches the hub about once a second. Two closer than this are a","+   * report delivered late (a long task in the game) or a client misbehaving:","+   * the later is dropped, and the next report, a second on, has the newest score.","+   */","+  progressMs: 250,","+  label: 24,","+});","+","+const FROM_GAME = new Set(['hello', 'ready', 'send', 'result', 'finish', 'error', 'progress', 'fullscreen', 'answer']);","+","+/** A progress report, checked: a finite score and an optional short label. Null when it is not one. */","+export function cleanProgress(p) {","+  if (!p || typeof p !== 'object') return null;","+  // A number, or text that is one: never null, '', true or [], which Number() would make 0 or 1.","+  const score = typeof p.score === 'number' || (typeof p.score === 'string' && p.score.trim() !== '') ? Number(p.score) : NaN;","+  if (!Number.isFinite(score)) return null;","+  const label = typeof p.label === 'string' ? p.label.trim().slice(0, LIMITS.label) : '';","+  return label ? { score, label } : { score };","+}","+","+/**","+ * @param {object} o","+ * @param {string} o.key              this player's key in the session","+ * @param {number} o.round","+ * @param {string} o.coordinator      key of whoever runs round.js","+ * @param {(msg:object) => void} o.post            to the game frame","+ * @param {{send:Function}} o.net","+ * @param {{now:()=>number}} [o.clock]             the coordinator's time, as seen here","+ * @param {(issue:{key:string, problem:string}) => void} [o.onIssue]","+ * @param {(id:number, progress:{score:number, label?:string}) => void} [o.onProgress]   a player's","+ *        progress, this one's included, for the hub's scoreboard; it never reaches the games","+ * @param {(on:boolean) => void} [o.onFullscreen]   the game asked for fullscreen (or out of it): the","+ *        hub's page takes it, so the hub's own cards stay over the game","+ * @param {(what:'ready'|'more') => void} [o.onAnswer]   this player answered on the game's own card","+ */","+export function createBridge({ key, round, coordinator, post, net, clock = Date, onIssue = () => {}, onProgress = () => {}, onFullscreen = () => {}, onAnswer = () => {} }) {","+  let welcomed = false;","+  let ended = false;","+  let started = false;","+  let helloSent = false;","+  let ownsCard = false;","+  let readySent = false;","+  let me = null;","+  let keys = [];","+  const gone = new Set();","+  const queue = [];","+  let queuedBytes = 0;","+  let tokens = LIMITS.burst;","+  let refilled = clock.now();","+  let progressAt = -Infinity;","+  const issues = [];","+  const stats = { sent: 0, received: 0, bytesSent: 0, dropped: 0 };","+","+  const toGame = (msg) => post({ aihub: 1, ...msg });","+  const toHub = (m) => net.send(coordinator, { k: 'c', r: round, m }, { reliable: true });","+  const issue = (problem) => {","+    const entry = { key, problem };","+    issues.push(entry);","+    onIssue(entry);","+  };","+","+  function fromGame(msg) {","+    if (!msg || msg.aihub !== 1) return;","+    if (!FROM_GAME.has(msg.type)) return issue(`unknown message type ${JSON.stringify(msg.type)}`);","+    if (msg.type === 'fullscreen') return onFullscreen(msg.on === true);","+    if (ended && msg.type !== 'error') return;","+    switch (msg.type) {","+      case 'hello':","+        if (helloSent) return;","+        helloSent = true;","+        ownsCard = msg.card === true;","+        return toHub({ type: 'hello', v: msg.v, client: String(msg.client || ''), mode: msg.mode ?? null, seats: msg.seats ?? null, card: ownsCard });","+      case 'ready':","+        if (!welcomed) return issue('ready before welcome');","+        readySent = true;","+        return toHub({ type: 'ready' });","+      case 'answer':","+        if (!ownsCard) return issue('answer without its own card: connect({ card: true })');","+        if (!welcomed || started) return;","+        if (msg.answer !== 'ready' && msg.answer !== 'more') return issue(`answer ${JSON.stringify(msg.answer)} is not ready or more`);","+        return onAnswer(msg.answer);","+      case 'result':","+        if (!welcomed) return issue('result before welcome');","+        return toHub({ type: 'result', time: msg.time, score: msg.score, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });","+      case 'finish':","+        if (!welcomed) return issue('finish before welcome');","+        return toHub({ type: 'finish', standings: msg.standings, scores: msg.scores, won: msg.won, stats: msg.stats, awards: msg.awards });","+      case 'error':","+        return toHub({ type: 'error', message: String(msg.message || '').slice(0, 500), fatal: msg.fatal === true });","+      case 'send':","+        return sendGame(msg);","+      case 'progress':","+        return sendProgress(msg);","+    }","+  }","+","+  /** Progress goes to this hub's scoreboard and to every other player's, never to a game. */","+  function sendProgress(msg) {","+    if (!welcomed) return issue('progress before welcome');","+    const p = cleanProgress(msg);","+    if (!p) return issue('progress needs a finite score');","+    const now = clock.now();","+    if (now - progressAt < LIMITS.progressMs) {","+      stats.dropped++;","+      return;","+    }","+    progressAt = now;","+    onProgress(me, p);","+    const envelope = { k: 'p', r: round, f: me, d: p };","+    for (const target of keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id))) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable: false });","+  }","+","+  function sendGame(msg) {","+    if (!welcomed) return issue('send before welcome');","+    let text;","+    try {","+      text = JSON.stringify(msg.data);","+    } catch {","+      return issue('send: data is not JSON');","+    }","+    if (text === undefined) return issue('send: no data');","+    if (text.length > LIMITS.maxBytes) {","+      stats.dropped++;","+      return issue(`send: ${text.length} bytes is over the ${LIMITS.maxBytes}-byte limit`);","+    }","+    const now = clock.now();","+    tokens = Math.min(LIMITS.burst, tokens + ((now - refilled) / 1000) * LIMITS.ratePerS);","+    refilled = now;","+    if (tokens < 1) {","+      stats.dropped++;","+      return issue(`send: over ${LIMITS.ratePerS} messages a second`);","+    }","+    tokens -= 1;","+    let targets;","+    if (msg.to === undefined || msg.to === null) {","+      targets = keys.filter((k, id) => id !== me && !gone.has(id));","+    } else {","+      if (!Number.isInteger(msg.to) || msg.to < 0 || msg.to >= keys.length || msg.to === me) {","+        return issue(`send: no player ${JSON.stringify(msg.to)} to send to`);","+      }","+      if (gone.has(msg.to)) return;","+      targets = [keys[msg.to]];","+    }","+    const reliable = msg.reliable !== false;","+    const envelope = { k: 'g', r: round, f: me, d: JSON.parse(text) };","+    for (const target of targets) net.send(target, envelope, { reliable });","+    stats.sent++;","+    stats.bytesSent += text.length;","+  }","+","+  function deliverGame(fromKey, env) {","+    if (ended || gone.has(env.f)) return;","+    if (keys[env.f] !== fromKey) return issue(`traffic from ${fromKey} claims to be player ${env.f}`);","+    stats.received++;","+    toGame({ type: 'message', from: env.f, data: env.d });","+  }","+","+  function fromNet(fromKey, env) {","+    if (!env || env.r !== round) return;","+    if (env.k === 'p') {","+      const p = cleanProgress(env.d);","+      if (welcomed && !ended && p && keys[env.f] === fromKey && !gone.has(env.f)) onProgress(env.f, p);","+      return;","+    }","+    if (env.k === 'g') {","+      if (welcomed) return deliverGame(fromKey, env);","+      const size = JSON.stringify(env.d ?? null).length;","+      if (queue.length >= LIMITS.queueMessages || queuedBytes + size > LIMITS.queueBytes) {","+        stats.dropped++;","+        return;","+      }","+      queue.push([fromKey, env]);","+      queuedBytes += size;","+      return;","+    }","+    if (env.k !== 'h' || fromKey !== coordinator || !env.m) return;","+    const m = env.m;","+    switch (m.type) {","+      case 'welcome': {","+        if (welcomed) return;","+        welcomed = true;","+        me = m.me;","+        keys = Array.isArray(m.keys) ? m.keys : [];","+        const { keys: _keys, round: _round, ...rest } = m;","+        // The limits ride in the welcome, so a client of 1.3.0 or later follows whatever this hub enforces.","+        toGame({ ...rest, round, limits: { maxBytes: LIMITS.maxBytes, ratePerS: LIMITS.ratePerS, burst: LIMITS.burst } });","+        for (const [k, e] of queue.splice(0)) deliverGame(k, e);","+        queuedBytes = 0;","+        return;","+      }","+      case 'start':","+        started = true;","+        return toGame({ type: 'start', in: Math.round(m.at - clock.now()) });","+      case 'leave':","+        gone.add(m.id);","+        return toGame({ type: 'leave', id: m.id, reason: m.reason });","+      case 'time-up':","+        return toGame({ type: 'time-up', graceMs: m.graceMs });","+      case 'end':","+        ended = true;","+        return toGame({ type: 'end', reason: m.reason, ...(m.standings ? { standings: m.standings } : {}) });","+    }","+  }","+","+  return {","+    key,","+    round,","+    fromGame,","+    fromNet,","+    /** The game's own card, while it is on: { left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked } (lib/hub/README.md, \"The card\"). */","+    card(state) {","+      if (ownsCard && welcomed && !started && !ended) toGame({ type: 'card', ...state });","+    },","+    /** The page holding this frame was hidden or shown: the coordinator watches the host's. */","+    visibility(hidden) {","+      if (helloSent && !ended) toHub({ type: 'vis', hidden: !!hidden });","+    },","+    issues,","+    stats,","+    get me() {","+      return me;","+    },","+    get ended() {","+      return ended;","+    },","+    /** The game shows its own card, and has loaded: the hub's card steps aside for it. */","+    get showsCard() {","+      return ownsCard && readySent && !ended;","+    },","+  };","+}","+","+/**","+ * Wire a bridge to an iframe: only messages from that frame's window count.","+ * Returns a function that unhooks it.","+ */","+export function attachFrame(frame, onMessage) {","+  const listener = (event) => {","+    if (event.source !== frame.contentWindow) return;","+    if (!event.data || event.data.aihub !== 1) return;","+    onMessage(event.data);","+  };","+  addEventListener('message', listener);","+  return () => removeEventListener('message', listener);","+}","+","+/** Post to a frame. The games may be served from anywhere, and nothing here is secret. */","+export const postTo = (frame) => (msg) => frame.contentWindow?.postMessage(msg, '*');","+","+/**","+ * A simulated network for the harness and tests: one-way latency with jitter,","+ * and loss for unreliable messages. Reliable messages stay in order per pair,","+ * as a WebRTC ordered channel would keep them.","+ */","+export function createLocalNetwork({ latency = 0, jitter = 0, loss = 0, random = Math.random, clock = globalThis } = {}) {","+  const endpoints = new Map();","+  const pairs = new Map(); // \"from\\0to\" -> reliable messages waiting, in send order","+  const now = () => (clock.performance?.now ? clock.performance.now() : Date.now());","+  const settings = { latency, jitter, loss };","+","+  const deliver = (from, to, target, copy) => {","+    if (endpoints.get(to) === target) for (const fn of target.listeners) fn(from, copy);","+  };","+","+  /** Reliable traffic leaves each pair's queue strictly in order, never before its time. */","+  function drain(pair) {","+    const q = pairs.get(pair);","+    q.timer = null;","+    while (q.items.length && q.items[0].at <= now() + 0.5) {","+      const { from, to, target, copy } = q.items.shift();","+      deliver(from, to, target, copy);","+    }","+    if (q.items.length) q.timer = clock.setTimeout(() => drain(pair), Math.max(1, Math.ceil(q.items[0].at - now())));","+  }","+","+  function endpoint(key) {","+    const listeners = new Set();","+    const self = {","+      key,","+      send(to, env, { reliable = true } = {}) {","+        const target = endpoints.get(to);","+        if (!target || !endpoints.has(key)) return;","+        if (!reliable && random() < settings.loss) return;","+        const copy = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(env));","+        const delay = to === key ? 0 : Math.max(0, settings.latency + (random() * 2 - 1) * settings.jitter);","+        if (!reliable) {","+          clock.setTimeout(() => deliver(key, to, target, copy), delay);","+          return;","+        }","+        const pair = `${key}\\u0000${to}`;","+        if (!pairs.has(pair)) pairs.set(pair, { items: [], timer: null });","+        const q = pairs.get(pair);","+        const last = q.items.at(-1)?.at ?? 0;","+        q.items.push({ at: Math.max(now() + delay, last), from: key, to, target, copy });","+        if (!q.timer) q.timer = clock.setTimeout(() => drain(pair), Math.ceil(delay));","+      },","+      onMessage(fn) {","+        listeners.add(fn);","+        return () => listeners.delete(fn);","+      },","+      close() {","+        endpoints.delete(key);","+      },","+      listeners,","+    };","+    endpoints.set(key, self);","+    return self;","+  }","+","+  return { endpoint, settings };","+}"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":2,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183638__x1295cd/work/KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183638/vendor/aihub/bridge.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183638__x1295cd/work/KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183638/vendor/aihub/harness.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183638__x1295cd/work/KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183638/vendor/aihub/round.js"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019HtPqU72BJDwgmFccw5nQg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2opsijaX4nLyPTinGh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PNBWjUzd3bLJk74R17zdpn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1002,1013p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-600; grep -n \"^- \\`game\\.\\(go\\|menu\\|pause\\|resume\\|lights\\|tween\\|script\\|after\\|setZoom\\|rotateView\\|yaw\\|zoom\\|freeze\\|flash\\|shake\\|scene\\b\\|sceneName\\|errors\\|weather\\|o\\b\\)\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-250 | head -30","description":"Read Suspicion fields and game method signatures"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5548,"cache_read_input_tokens":207732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5548},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"b26d44ba-1f42-4ec6-a38b-b3a09db98f0b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:26.223Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2opeq7X48wH8UMds8x","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PNBWjUzd3bLJk74R17zdpn":{"command":"sed -n 1002,1013p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-600; grep -n \"^- \\`game\\.\\(go\\|menu\\|pause\\|resume\\|lights\\|tween\\|script\\|after\\|setZoom\\|rotateView\\|yaw\\|zoom\\|freeze\\|flash\\|shake\\|scene\\b\\|sceneName\\|errors\\|weather\\|o\\b\\)\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-250 | head -30","description":"Read Suspicion fields and game method signatures"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNBWjUzd3bLJk74R17zdpn","type":"tool_result","content":"- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget seconds. Each step: suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)\n- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n- `suspicion.level = 0` †: 0..1.2, how suspicious\n- `suspicion.since = 0` †: seconds since it last saw or heard anything\n- `suspicion.state = 'calm'` †: 'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'\n366:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n367:- `game.lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` †: something that blocks light (GPU shadows): a cylinder of radius r from the floor up to height top\n368:- `game.lights.heat(x, y, z, width, strength = 1)` †: heat shimmer above a point (GPU only). width in world units, strength ~0.5..1.5\n369:- `game.lights.on` †: true when the canvas lighting draws this frame: enabled, or standing in for GPU lighting the game turned on that can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view); gpu.fallback = false keeps such a frame unlit\n370:- `game.lights.refresh()` †: rebuild the darkness bands after changing dark, levels or glow (lights.dark = [r, g, b]; lights.refresh())\n371:- `game.lights.render(r)` †: darken the frame by the lights (the renderer calls it after the queue, when enabled)\n372:- `game.lights.ambient = .15` †: how lit unlit places are, 0 (black) .. 1\n373:- `game.lights.dark = [10, 6, 24]` †: the color of darkness, [r, g, b]\n374:- `game.lights.darkness = .9` †: how dark the darkest places get, 0..1 (the smooth style, E.style.trans 'alpha')\n375:- `game.lights.enabled = false` †: false (the default) turns the canvas lighting off\n376:- `game.lights.glow = [255, 200, 140, 0]` †: the color, [r, g, b, a], where light is brightest\n377:- `game.lights.glowAt = 1.7` †: the light level (1 = fully lit) above which it glows\n378:- `game.lights.levels = [.9, .7, .48, .26, .08, 0]` †: the darkness of each lighting band, darkest first (dithered between them)\n379:- `game.lights.list = []` †: this frame's lights from add()\n380:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n381:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n470:- `game.after(seconds, fn)`: run fn once after `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change. Returns { cancel() }\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n481:- `game.freeze(s)`: hit-stop: the game stands still for s seconds (.04-.08 for a hit); input still ticks\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris',\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu(\n489:- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n493:- `game.resume()`: take the game out of pause (and close the pause screen)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a nu\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and l\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n508:- `game.tween(target, to, seconds, o)` †: ease target's numbers to new values over seconds of game time: game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat (more plays; -1 forever), yoyo (every other play runs back), onDone(target),\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, \n512:- `game.zoomRange()` †: the zooms the player may take the camera to here, [min, max] (the scene's camera.zoom, or the game's; a function of the game gives one per screen shape or level), or null where they can't (camera.zoom false or none)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"59f63453-0e36-46ad-aeb9-9da2ec510397","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:26.729Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget seconds. Each step: suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)\n- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n- `suspicion.level = 0` †: 0..1.2, how suspicious\n- `suspicion.since = 0` †: seconds since it last saw or heard anything\n- `suspicion.state = 'calm'` †: 'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'\n366:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n367:- `game.lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` †: something that blocks light (GPU shadows): a cylinder of radius r from the floor up to height top\n368:- `game.lights.heat(x, y, z, width, strength = 1)` †: heat shimmer above a point (GPU only). width in world units, strength ~0.5..1.5\n369:- `game.lights.on` †: true when the canvas lighting draws this frame: enabled, or standing in for GPU lighting the game turned on that can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view); gpu.fallback = false keeps such a frame unlit\n370:- `game.lights.refresh()` †: rebuild the darkness bands after changing dark, levels or glow (lights.dark = [r, g, b]; lights.refresh())\n371:- `game.lights.render(r)` †: darken the frame by the lights (the renderer calls it after the queue, when enabled)\n372:- `game.lights.ambient = .15` †: how lit unlit places are, 0 (black) .. 1\n373:- `game.lights.dark = [10, 6, 24]` †: the color of darkness, [r, g, b]\n374:- `game.lights.darkness = .9` †: how dark the darkest places get, 0..1 (the smooth style, E.style.trans 'alpha')\n375:- `game.lights.enabled = false` †: false (the default) turns the canvas lighting off\n376:- `game.lights.glow = [255, 200, 140, 0]` †: the color, [r, g, b, a], where light is brightest\n377:- `game.lights.glowAt = 1.7` †: the light level (1 = fully lit) above which it glows\n378:- `game.lights.levels = [.9, .7, .48, .26, .08, 0]` †: the darkness of each lighting band, darkest first (dithered between them)\n379:- `game.lights.list = []` †: this frame's lights from add()\n380:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n381:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n470:- `game.after(seconds, fn)`: run fn once after `seconds` of game time. Cleared on scene change. Returns { cancel() }\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n481:- `game.freeze(s)`: hit-stop: the game stands still for s seconds (.04-.08 for a hit); input still ticks\n482:- `game.go(name, data, o = {})`: switch scene: game.go('play', { level: 2 }). It fades through black (dithered) unless opts.fade is 0 (a cut) or another number of seconds; opts.fade can name a transition instead: 'black', 'white', 'wipe', 'iris',\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu(\n489:- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n493:- `game.resume()`: take the game out of pause (and close the pause screen)\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a nu\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and l\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n508:- `game.tween(target, to, seconds, o)` †: ease target's numbers to new values over seconds of game time: game.tween(door, { y: 40 }, .5, { ease: 'outBack', delay, repeat (more plays; -1 forever), yoyo (every other play runs back), onDone(target),\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, \n512:- `game.zoomRange()` †: the zooms the player may take the camera to here, [min, max] (the scene's camera.zoom, or the game's; a function of the game gives one per screen shape or level), or null where they can't (camera.zoom false or none)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":203,"oldLines":3,"newStart":203,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":300,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"c01df684-66f3-4ac5-bbbc-2112b349a7dc\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":4900,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"e4fabdf5-35c6-407a-b980-466fe921800b\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":5150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"44ba21ac-c110-4ef3-ac89-84b258e8328d\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":5350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"30117c1e-b919-4811-aaed-4de99f9a4ee3\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183606__xf7f297/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":110,"oldLines