{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FQ3gokKbe3s96xxmnkxyKd","type":"tool_result","content":"276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a \n284:- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n285:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n287:- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n291:- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n300:- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n301:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n304:- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n305:- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n312:- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n313:- `input.suppressCode(code)` †: A widget owns this button; other devices bound to the same action still work.\n314:- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n321:- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy)\n322:- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n327:- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"8836ab52-8a4c-495d-93d1-b5482c572235","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:41:43.190Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"276:- `input.anyPressed()`: any action pressed this step (title screens: \"press any button\")\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a \n284:- `input.consume(a)`: mark a buffered press of action a as used, so buffered(a) is false until the next press\n285:- `input.consumeAll()`: forget every pending press (after closing a menu or dialog, so the same press does not also attack)\n287:- `input.down(a)`: is the action held right now?\n291:- `input.hold(a, on = true)`: hold an action down (on) or let it go (false), as its key would\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n300:- `input.press(code)`: press a key or button code ('KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:attack') as if the person did: scripted input, tests, bots\n301:- `input.pressed(a)`: true only during the first update step after the press (menus, jumps, one-shot actions)\n304:- `input.release(code)`: let go of a code pressed with press()\n305:- `input.released(a)`: true only during the first update step after the action was let go\n312:- `input.suppress(a)` †: Suppress a held action until the next tick (a HUD widget owns the pointer this step).\n313:- `input.suppressCode(code)` †: A widget owns this button; other devices bound to the same action still work.\n314:- `input.tap(a)`: press an action for one update step, as a quick tap of its key (scripted input, tests, an AI): pressed() and down() are true in the next step, released() in the one after\n321:- `input.zoom()` †: the camera zoom the player asked for since the last step, as a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther; 1: none): the wheel, - and = and a pinch, where the scene lets them zoom. The game applies it (game.zoomBy)\n322:- `input.zoomPoint()` †: [x, y] where the last zoom was asked for: the mouse pointer for the wheel, between the fingers for a pinch; null when the keys zoomed (about the screen's middle)\n327:- `input.held`: the key and button codes down right now ('KeyD', 'Mouse0', 'Pad0', 'Act:jump')","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FQ3gokKbe3s96xxmnkxyKd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
