{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8HSVgdam5NCyz2dhNt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm stopping here. The checker now wants testing on real controller hardware and a physical touch screen, plus a feature audit done by someone other than me. None of that can happen in this environment: it has no gamepad, no touch screen and no visible browser, and TASK.md forbids using subagents or workflows to audit. Rerunning the checks I've already done won't change that.\n\nThe rest of the goal is met:\n- The game file `Bentou2BirthOfTheLunchboxAssassins-Tenchu2BirthOfTheStealthAssassins-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183420.html` is in the folder root and matches TASK.md's name pattern.\n- `exit-interview.json` parses and every field is filled.\n- 165 automated checks pass on the final file, including the real AI Hub test harness and a Chromium run of the controller, keyboard and mouse requirements with a simulated DualSense controller.\n- `FEATURES.md` maps each TASK.md requirement to its code and the test that covers it, as my own audit.\n\nTo close the remaining gap:\n1. Play the HTML file with a real DualSense or Xbox controller and on a touch-only device.\n2. Have someone check `FEATURES.md` against TASK.md.\n\nIf that's not worth doing, you can clear the goal with `/goal clear`.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:34:20\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Third-person ninja stealth-action with melee combat and boss duels. Isometric third person, turnable in 45° steps and zoomable, with a high three-quarter camera option.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine with nine small patches, AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript in one HTML file. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art (320×240, stretched to fill the screen). New character gear, Japanese props and materials written as shape data, and canvas lighting.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural character animation, plus new Silent Cut moves (5 kinds × 2 characters), grapple, riposte, ninja run, wall hug, swimming, eating, and a four-legged hound.\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth: layered Japanese-scale music, sound effects made in code, and a gibberish voice synth for spoken lines.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1–4 players. Offline, the Shadow Trial lets you race your own best run.\n- **Testing:** One command runs every suite and prints only failures and a count; 165 checks pass.\n  - Headless suites cover mechanics, all four missions, menus, the story, attract mode, Dev Mode, the Workshop, a mock AI Hub, and determinism.\n  - Browser checks cover the game file, the input audit with a simulated controller, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** The engine handoff docs and the AI Hub README, plus the planner's research carried in PLAN.md.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 12 real issues, all fixed:\n   - Guards counted the hero's visibility twice.\n   - The from-above Silent Cut never triggered.\n   - Diving was impossible.\n   - Guards got stuck on props.\n   - A held button didn't count as activity, so the demo could start while you held it.\n   - The camera lagged behind teleports in slow motion.\n   - The mouse never took over again after a gamepad was used.\n   - The Workshop missed quick key taps.\n   - The mouse wheel was ignored during an attack.\n   - The rest were mistakes in the tests' own setup.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 3: no diving, guards stuck on props, and the double-counted visibility.\n3. **Most helpful test:** The missions suite, which completes all four missions through their real objectives.\n4. **Least helpful test:** The headless random-input smoke test, because headless runs skip all drawing.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** How much already works headless: movement, perception, paired actions, standard menus, and fixed-step tests.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. Crouch is a held state rather than a toggle, pathfinding ignores props, the sight check already includes the target's visibility, a one-step press can be lost during hit-stop, and custom input maps must restate the menu keys.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** The stealth layer: Shadow Sight, the Ki gauge, light maps, guard behaviour, Silent Cuts, the bosses, and the mission runtime.\n4. **Hardest part:** Learning how existing systems behave in a 1.2 MB engine, since those details live only in the source.\n5. **What I changed:** Nine small patches, listed in `engine/PATCHES.md`: PlayStation button symbols in the font, a PlayStation/Xbox symbol setting, new character gear, settings rows on custom menu screens, hover moves focus, interface scaling for TV distance, plucked-string notes, a voice volume channel, and leaving the hub's Create + Options shortcut to the hub.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** Make pathfinding respect solid props.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** It's concrete about the player: a TV at 10 feet, button symbols, attract mode, touch-only devices, dev sliders and the hub.\n2. **What was confusing:** The bracketed file-name pattern versus the plan's own names, and how to weigh \"every feature\" against a plan far larger than one session.\n3. **Hardest thing:** The scope of the game within one session.\n4. **What I'd change:** Mark which features are must-haves and which are stretch goals, give a session budget and a worked file-name example, and mention the temp-disk limit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3092,"cache_read_input_tokens":667479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3092},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"20301708-a3f6-4774-bac5-2d4940e82150","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:49:28.383Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh8HSAbBLhgMLwTi2cDr"}
