{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8K1ULS9RN49dWJnifS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I re-checked the condition as written: it asks for every feature to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. That holds for every TASK.md requirement. Controller and touch support use the browser's standard Gamepad and pointer APIs. I verified them in Chromium with a simulated standard-mapping pad and touch emulation; they have not been tried on a real controller or phone.\n\n**TASK.md features and where they are checked:**\n- **Single-file game.** `Bentou2BirthOfTheLunchboxAssassins-Tenchu2BirthOfTheStealthAssassins-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183420.html` is in the root. It boots from `file://` with no errors.\n- **Complete demo.** A training mission and three story missions, each with a boss, all completed by tests through their real objectives. It also includes:\n  - stealth (light, noise, Shadow Sight, the Ki gauge) and Silent Cuts from five directions;\n  - grapple, swimming and diving, wall hug, and dragging bodies;\n  - 10 tools, alarm bells and reinforcements, an escort and a timer;\n  - ranks, unlocks and saves, the Workshop editor, and the Shadow Trial.\n- **Dev mode.** Opened from the pause menu, with cheats, teleports, debug views and 32 live balance sliders with reset. Verified in Chromium by moving a slider and resetting it.\n- **Attract mode.** Starts after 10 s idle and cycles 7 demo scenes; any input exits. Three full loops run without errors, in tests and in the browser.\n- **Multiplayer.** AI Hub ghost mode for 1–4 players with the game's own pre-round card. The real AI Hub harness passes with 2 players, with 4 players on a lossy network, and when the host leaves.\n- **Controller-first, 10-foot UI.**\n  - PlayStation button symbols by default, with an Xbox option.\n  - Prompts follow the last device used.\n  - Keyboard and mouse work natively: hover moves the focus, the wheel cycles tools, the mouse aims and paints in the editor.\n  - The interface scales for a TV.\n- **Touch-only devices.** Show \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button, and attract mode still runs.\n- **Code, audio and tone.** The source has no TODOs, placeholders or stub functions; the build refuses to compile if any appear. All audio is generated in code, including gibberish voices. The writing follows the source's terse feudal-drama tone.\n- **Records.** About/Credits holds the four sections below, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field answered.\n\nAll 165 automated checks pass.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:34:20\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Third-person ninja stealth-action with melee combat and boss duels. Isometric third person, turnable in 45° steps and zoomable, with a high three-quarter camera option.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine with nine small patches, AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript in one HTML file. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art, expanded to fill the screen. New character gear, Japanese props and materials written as shape data, and canvas lighting.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs and actions, plus new Silent Cut choreographies (5 kinds × 2 characters), grapple, riposte, ninja run, wall hug, swimming, eating, and a quadruped hound.\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth: layered Japanese-scale music, sound effects made in code, and a gibberish voice synth for every spoken line.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1–4 players. Offline, the Shadow Trial lets you race your own best run.\n- **Testing:** One command runs every suite and prints only failures and a one-line count; 165 checks pass.\n  - Headless suites cover mechanics, all missions, the menus and story, attract mode, Dev Mode, the Workshop, a mock AI Hub, and determinism.\n  - Browser checks cover the bundle, a controls audit using a simulated DualSense plus keyboard and mouse, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** The engine handoff docs and the AI Hub README, plus the planner's research carried in PLAN.md.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 12 real issues, all fixed. Among them: guards squared the hero's exposure, the from-above Silent Cut never triggered, diving was impossible, guards got stuck on props, held input didn't count against the idle timer, the camera lagged teleports, the mouse never took over after a pad was used, the Workshop missed quick taps, and the wheel was ignored mid-attack. The rest were test-setup mistakes.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 3: no diving, guards stuck on props, and the squared exposure.\n3. **Most helpful test:** The missions suite, which completes all four missions through their real objectives.\n4. **Least helpful test:** The headless random-input smoke test, because headless runs skip drawing.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** How much already works headless: movement, perception, paired actions, standard menus, and fixed-step tests.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - an intent's crouch is a state, not a toggle;\n   - flow fields ignore props;\n   - the sight check already includes the target's exposure;\n   - a one-step press can be lost during hit-stop;\n   - a custom input map must restate the menu keys.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** The stealth layer: Shadow Sight, the Ki gauge, light maps, guard behaviour, Silent Cuts, the bosses, and the mission runtime.\n4. **Hardest part:** Learning how existing systems behave in a 1.2 MB engine, since the details live only in the source.\n5. **What I changed:** Nine small patches, listed in `engine/PATCHES.md`:\n   - PlayStation glyphs in the pixel font, and a PlayStation/Xbox button setting;\n   - new character gear;\n   - settings rows on custom menu screens, hover moves focus, and 10-foot UI scaling;\n   - plucked-string music notes and a voice volume bus;\n   - a pause guard so the hub's Create + Options shortcut doesn't pause the game.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** Make flow fields respect solid props.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** It's concrete about the player: a TV at 10 feet, button glyphs, attract mode, touch-only devices, dev sliders and the hub.\n2. **What was confusing:** The bracketed file-name pattern versus the plan's own names, and how to weigh \"every feature\" against a plan larger than one session.\n3. **Hardest thing:** The scope within one session.\n4. **What I'd change:** Mark must-have versus stretch features, give a session budget and a worked file-name example, and mention the temp-disk limit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2593,"cache_read_input_tokens":670571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2593},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea","uuid":"7d770b5a-f7d5-4fa3-965b-379a33d4db95","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:49:53.799Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh8K18zWDh5y6nyvdsmm"}
